{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5","id":1417630,"title":"What do you think of the Lasombra joining the Camarilla in V5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-11T07:21:51-07:00","id":1417630,"title":"What do you think of the Lasombra joining the Camarilla in V5?","content":"Or for that matter what about the overall collapse of the Sabbat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T07:27:21-07:00","id":1417631,"title":"","content":"I think it's mostly a meta reflection of how people want to play as the &quot;villain&quot; clans, and this gives a big lore reason for why Lasombra are playable without being Sabbat.<br /> <br /> In terms of that, I think it's good. I still think Lasombra attracts a <i>certain kind</i> of player, but that's somebody else's problem. I predict that something similar is going to happen to the Tzimisce (ie, some sort of lore justification as to why 'standard' player clans can play Tzimisce).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T07:31:50-07:00","id":1417632,"title":"","content":"It makes perfect sense to me within the context of the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T07:47:31-07:00","id":1417635,"title":"","content":"both the lasombra and Camarilla have been reduced to boken versions of themselves<br /> <br /> it's not really the lasombra joining the Camarilla,<br /> it's a sect fallen from grace being joined by a clan who's just a shadow of its former self<br /> <br /> as for the sabbat,<br /> during their first interview, the devs said the sabbat would be put aside along with elders (god knows why),<br /> and that's what they did<br /> <br /> <br /> overall, I don't mind it as a small spin-off scenario,<br /> however, after two years, this is what is being maintained in both the books and the video games<br /> <br /> considering I was hyped for the games, it seems I won't be enjoying them as much as I had hoped","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T07:59:05-07:00","id":1417636,"title":"","content":"It's basically nonsense and goes against everything we know about Lasombra's lore.<br /> <br /> As for the Sabbat... It's a bloody crime against players. You like Sabbat? Too bad for you. Sabbat has always been the second biggest group (both lore-wise both published-supplements-wise), and now It Is gone, and Sabbat players are left hanging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-11-2020, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T08:29:13-07:00","id":1417638,"title":"","content":"Needless to say, I disagree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12142\" data-vbnamecard=\"12142\">Undead rabbit</a><br /> <br /> The Lasombra joining the Camarilla was a move I never expected to happen in my games as the previous editions seemed to establish their control of the Sabbat was all powerful and that the Antitribu were basically just cannon fodder for them. In a very real way, the Lasombra <i>were</i> the Sabbat so them defecting to the Camarilla feels like more a statement of, &quot;Stick a stake in it, the Sabbat are done now&quot; than the Gehenna War ever did.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I feel like it also reflects a lot of changing realities in the new millennium, changes in the fanbase, and works well with the metaplot. I was initially very skeptical but the argument for the premise persuaded me in <i>Chicago by Night</i> persuaded me both in as well as out of universe.<br /> My thoughts can be summarized as such:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>A lot of Camarilla fans love the Lasombra.</b> It's one of the single most popular clans in V:TM. A lot of these fans are Camarilla potlickers and intrigue courtly types. It doesn't make sense to state they're constantly hunted and on the run with them wanting to be in the high society part of the setting. Cynthia Marie initially wanted Nelli G to be a Lasombra and Eb's actress, well, ALSO wanted to be a Lasombra. The majority of online tabletop groups seem to have one Lasombra or another.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>V5's vampires are a lot closer to being Sabbat</b>. The Anarchs are a lot more murderous Lost Boys and Near Dark rednecks than idealists. There's a lot more open Caine worship and weird cults in general. The Camarilla has a lot more weird Gehenna sects. Everyone's just a lot more openly evil. As such, the Sabbat doesn't feel quite as necessary as it did in previous editions.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>&quot;The Sacrifice&quot; is a really good scenario</b>: It allows the PCs to play a big role in determining whether the Lasombra join the Camarilla or not.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>The Lasombra help shore up the Camarilla</b>: The Camarilla losing the Brujah and Gangrel but gaining the Banu Haqim and Lasombra makes it so the Camarilla is back to full strength. So they don't look like chumps.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Only half the Lasombra defected anyway</b>: Part of what I note is the Lasombra Archbishops, Cardinals, and so on didn't defect. Only the people who had nothing to lose or felt they had a lot to gain defected. The Lasombra clan culture is so scheming and ruthless that the idea they'd stay where they couldn't get power is silly.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>There needed to be consequences for Beckett's Jyhad Diary</b>: The Lasombra Antediluvian is revealed to be alive at the climax of that book. This undermined the entire argument of the Lasombra for the Sabbat's existence. If it's still alive, then they've utterly failed to fight the Antediluvians. If you take a shot at the Devil and miss, you need to rethink your life choices, especially if your sect is based around the argument, &quot;I shot the Devil and killed him.&quot;<br /> <br /> 7. <b>It's already lead to some awesome stories</b>: We've already got <i>Shadows of New York</i> and an extensive LA by Night campaign about the Lasombra defection. I love Julia and her story is all about her winning status for the Lasombra in New York.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Personal Bias</b>: I play in Tampa, Florida (despite living in Kentucky) with my Florida group and the setting for that in my games was it was &quot;the sole Lasombra Antitribu run city in America.&quot; Most of my players were Lasombra Antitribu so it certainly was a good idea for my game and added some twists and turns.<br /> <br /> Now, for the Gehenna Crusade?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I feel like this needs to be brought to an end. Theres no reason for to just have the Sabbat walk off the board like that and even if you didn't like them, they were an important part of the game. Having the Sabbat have a really bad decade or two? Another Sabbat Civil War? Lose a lot of territory? Fine. However, the Sabbat just vanishing like the Tremere Antitribu is silly.<br /> <br /> I'm glad the <b>Seven Fires</b> exist and kind of hope that Onyx Path Publishing expands on them into a micro-sect under White Wolf's radar if they're really determined to keep the Sabbat dead and gone. At least give players the option to play something distinctly Sabbat like. Also, Sabbat are useful as antagonists when you don't have a game planned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2020, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T08:42:00-07:00","id":1417642,"title":"","content":"It works on a meta level, or out of game level, because it opens up play possibilities and maintains in-game tension. In game I am also alright with it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Something that is lost sight of in these discussions <i>is that not all the Lasombra have joined the Camarilla</i>. Enough have joined for them to be a viable clan option for players, but many of them are still in whatever remains of the Sabbat or working as independent operators. This means there should be enmity between the Camarilla Lasombra and all the other's not in the Ivory Tower. Of course, the same thing is true of the Banu Haqim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-11-2020, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T08:43:02-07:00","id":1417643,"title":"","content":"I like the Idea of more Lasombra in the Camarilla. <br /> This is not how you do it. <br /> <br /> 1- Viniculum. You can't just get up and leave the Sabbat. That's half of what makes them work. <br /> 2- The Sabbat got written off with absurd reasoning. The gut-feeling is to be defensive whenever V5 does anything to do with the Sabbat. If they truly felt they were leading a ship heading for it's doom maybe they should have fucking lead the ship properly. <br /> 3- Better to rule in hell than be a slave in heaven; Why would the Lasombra give up their position of leaders in the Sabbat to take up the 4 point 'probationary sect member' flaw? To be the runts of the litter? To put their lives in the hands of a sect which has long wished them ill? <br /> 4-The Clan curse and oblivion. You'd think this would be a seperate matter, but I think it's indicative of how the writers see lasombra; They don't like lasombra. They want to punish people who like lasombra. Sure, the clan attracts <i>that guy</i> but you're being <i>that guy</i> for taking a favoured toy and smearing it with shit. The new clan weakness is utterly hostile to the archetypal Lasombra: A highly independent professional who &quot;gets shit done&quot; and works behind the scenes falls apart when they need a fucking nursemaid to take their calls for them (not to mention how fucking outrageously <i>modern </i>such a weakness is) and then their three disciplines, including their signature discipline, were utterly neutered. It really seems like someone tired of 'that guy' playing Lasombra so much they made their absolute damnedest that the clan would be regulated to absolute-bitch whipping boy. They suck to play, they're in a politically shit position, and the Ravnos didn't even get it half as hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T08:44:26-07:00","id":1417644,"title":"","content":"I think Lasobra fit just right with the new, more &quot;elite&quot; Camarilla. If they joined the &quot;all-are-welcome&quot; Cam from before V5, I would have objections.<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind, which is &quot;Sabbat is going to bleed themselves in the Gehenna Crusade, so we'll just jump ship, cause we were always 'winners' not 'losers' clan&quot; sits well with their &quot;social Darwinism&quot; philosophy. Yes, they were a part of Sabbat, because during the CoT they did not want to surrender to Cam dictating them what to do, but it was over 500 years ago. The situation is different.<br /> <br /> As probably the majority of players, I'm in the &quot;I want to know the exact Sabbat status quo&quot; club, but I also can understand that they want to give them some time-off, so new Camarilla and the Anarchs can have some fun on their own. And I do believe that both elders and Sabbat will return to take what is theirs. Why would they even bother to hire Justin Achilli back if not for that reason alone.<br /> <br /> We just have to wait this year or two to see Player's Guide, so other countries' publishers can publish their stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T08:46:46-07:00","id":1417645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417643#post1417643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Idea of more Lasombra in the Camarilla.<br /> This is not how you do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, couple of points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1- Viniculum. You can't just get up and leave the Sabbat. That's half of what makes them work. </div> </div> </div>Technically, everytime someone leaves the Sabbat, that means that they're going to bring someone along with them. The Vinculum doesn't instill Sabbat loyalty, it instills fanatical loyalty among the group and if the guy with the most loyalty leaves them he takes everyone with him. Which makes the defection = Civil War make more sense because if a majority of Lasombra are defecting then they have an army to help them do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2- The Sabbat got written off with absurd reasoning. The gut-feeling is to be defensive whenever V5 does anything to do with the Sabbat. If they truly felt they were leading a ship heading for it's doom maybe they should have fucking lead the ship properly. </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of the Gehenna Crusade. It's one of my two main issues along with the handling of Elder Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3- Better to rule in hell than be a slave in heaven; Why would the Lasombra give up their position of leaders in the Sabbat to take up the 4 point 'probationary sect member' flaw? To be the runts of the litter? To put their lives in the hands of a sect which has long wished them ill? </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra saw the Camarilla was weak and that they could seize control of it from the Ventrue. Given what we've seen, I think the Lasombra are destined to be No. 2# much quicker than the Banu Haqim and the Ventrue are going to have to fight tooth and nail to keep them from No. 1.<br /> <br /> Or, to paraphrase Milton, &quot;Better to conquer Heaven than rule in Hell.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4-The Clan curse and oblivion. You'd think this would be a seperate matter, but I think it's indicative of how the writers see lasombra; They don't like lasombra. They want to punish people who like lasombra. Sure, the clan attracts <i>that guy</i> but you're being <i>that guy</i> for taking a favoured toy and smearing it with shit. The new clan weakness is utterly hostile to the archetypal Lasombra: A highly independent professional who &quot;gets shit done&quot; and works behind the scenes falls apart when they need a fucking nursemaid to take their calls for them (not to mention how fucking outrageously <i>modern </i>such a weakness is) and then their three disciplines, including their signature discipline, were utterly neutered. It really seems like someone tired of 'that guy' playing Lasombra so much they made their absolute damnedest that the clan would be regulated to absolute-bitch whipping boy. They suck to play, they're in a politically shit position, and the Ravnos didn't even get it half as hard. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Lasombra have always had the ghoul who dresses them like it's the 19th century. I'm not a fan of the technocracy weakness, though, because every Lasombra needs a jet black or white sports car.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T09:10:09-07:00","id":1417648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417645#post1417645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">e leaves the Sabbat, that means that they're going to bring someone along with them. The Vinculum doesn't instill Sabbat loyalty, it instills fanatical loyalty among the group and if the guy with the most loyalty leaves them he takes everyone with him. Which makes the defection = Civil War make more sense because if a majority of Lasombra are defecting then they have an army to help them do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they'd come over with their entire packs, who usually aren't only-lasombra. Don't you realise how much of a threat that is? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lasombra saw the Camarilla was weak and that they could seize control of it from the Ventrue. Given what we've seen, I think the Lasombra are destined to be No. 2# much quicker than the Banu Haqim and the Ventrue are going to have to fight tooth and nail to keep them from No. 1.<br /> <br /> Or, to paraphrase Milton, &quot;Better to conquer Heaven than rule in Hell.&quot; </div> </div> </div> I know they often suffer from delusions of granduer, but they clearly cannot compete with the Ventrue on the Ventrue's home turf. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be fair, the Lasombra have always had the ghoul who dresses them like it's the 19th century. I'm not a fan of the technocracy weakness, though, because every Lasombra needs a jet black or white sports car. </div> </div> </div>The obsession with looking right was always the thing of 'a few lasombra' rather than the whole clan, and mirrors kinda working for them not takes away some of it. Needing an intermediary for a phone call is something else. While it can work for some Lasombra, it really doesn't work for others; They had Potence and Obtenebration in addition to Dominate because sometimes, they like to Get Shit Done themselves. Most clan weaknesses encourage vampires to play according to their disciplines, with the Lasombra there's considerable clash between weakness and disciplines. <br /> <br /> As for the Car, I think most are likely to prefer luxury vehicles, though sports cars aren't unheard of, so are serial killer vans. We can agree on the colouration. <br /> Their suit choices will leave much to be desired in the Camarilla. The Tremere might approve, but the Toreador and Ventrue scorn all the black.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T09:46:43-07:00","id":1417653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417642#post1417642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Something that is lost sight of in these discussions <i>is that not all the Lasombra have joined the Camarilla</i>. Enough have joined for them to be a viable clan option for players, but many of them are still in whatever remains of the Sabbat or working as independent operators. This means there should be enmity between the Camarilla Lasombra and all the other's not in the Ivory Tower. Of course, the same thing is true of the Banu Haqim.</div> </div> </div> </div>except none of this gets featured anywhere<br /> <br /> what does it matter that there are still lasombra in the sabbat when the sabbat hardly gets featured or get any mechanics on top of being reduced to dumpster diving thugs in the lore?<br /> <br /> while you and Phipps get to have fun with your Chicagos, your Al Capones and Bahari and whatnot,<br /> all we, fans of dark prophets, Jailors of the demiurge and soul stealing crusaders get is...Samson<br /> <br /> the last VtM VN featured spectres...spectres from WtO,<br /> meanwhile, the sabbat from VtM...nowhere to be seen...probably dumpster diving in the background","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T09:51:52-07:00","id":1417654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417653#post1417653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> except none of this gets featured anywhere<br /> <br /> what does it matter that there are still lasombra in the sabbat when the sabbat hardly gets featured or get any mechanics on top of being reduced to dumpster diving thugs in the lore?<br /> <br /> while you and Phipps get to have fun with your Chicagos, your Al Capones and Bahari and whatnot,<br /> all we, fans of dark prophets, Jailors of the demiurge and soul stealing crusaders get is...Samson</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess to never imagining in my wildest dreams that Samson would be making his return and being actually terrifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the last VtM VN featured spectres...spectres from WtO </div> </div> </div>There's a W:TO and W:TA game coming out too so the old World of Darkness is gradually returning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> meanwhile, the sabbat from VtM...nowhere to be seen...probably dumpster diving in the background </div> </div> </div>One of the things I've tried to do as Moderator is reframe the conversation because, again, there's no need to think of this as a conflict between Editions. You can like some elements of the changes and dislike others.<br /> <br /> I very much agree that the Sabbat should make their return and am genuinely surprised that we haven't gotten anything regarding them other than their tiny bit of information in <b>The Chicago Folio</b>. There's been ex-Sabbat, Sabbat defectors, and other people left and right but most of the material we've seen has only alluded to what's going on with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> As much as I love Anarchs and the new changes, I do think they should have included all of the Clans in the main book and given at least a short write-up of the Sabbat. I think fans would appreciate even a smaller, more vicious inhuman Sabbat than just wiping them off the board. I was intrigued by the write-up of Sabbat in CBN and would like to see more.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that Lucita may have been Final Deathed because they had her defect from the Antitribu to the &quot;normal&quot; Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2020, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T10:02:36-07:00","id":1417656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417648#post1417648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, they'd come over with their entire packs, who usually aren't only-lasombra. Don't you realise how much of a threat that is?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely interesting to speculate how many Antitribu have come over to the Camarilla without them ever suspecting. The Lasombra have potentially a huge number of allies with plenty of them having experience infiltrating Camarilla cities that can just show up and say, &quot;Hi, my name is Bob. I'm a Brujah an....d I'm happy to be here!&quot; If their Vinculum isn't very strong, they might also be the first to betray them and stake them too because the price for entry is one Sabbat older than yourself.<br /> <br /> And who is going to question you about ages?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know they often suffer from delusions of granduer, but they clearly cannot compete with the Ventrue on the Ventrue's home turf. </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I think the Lasombra are willing to play the long game. The Lasombra have potential allies in the Banu Haqim and the Tremere are no longer supporting the Ventrue like they used to.<br /> <br /> Because the Ventrue did jack for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The obsession with looking right was always the thing of 'a few lasombra' rather than the whole clan, and mirrors kinda working for them not takes away some of it. Needing an intermediary for a phone call is something else. While it can work for some Lasombra, it really doesn't work for others; They had Potence and Obtenebration in addition to Dominate because sometimes, they like to Get Shit Done themselves. Most clan weaknesses encourage vampires to play according to their disciplines, with the Lasombra there's considerable clash between weakness and disciplines. </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I find the technology weakness very unforgiving in the 21st century and doesn't really fit my view of them. I do think the Lasombra having lots of mortal servants makes sense, though, and I never liked the Sabbat's, &quot;We're all vampires and accumulating mortal power is SILLY!&quot;<br /> <br /> It makes me think the Grimaldi should have joined Pentex years ago or become a Giovanni family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Car, I think most are likely to prefer luxury vehicles, though sports cars aren't unheard of, so are serial killer vans. We can agree on the colouration.<br /> Their suit choices will leave much to be desired in the Camarilla. The Tremere might approve, but the Toreador and Ventrue scorn all the black. </div> </div> </div>This is both true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T10:40:50-07:00","id":1417657,"title":"","content":"I think this is one of the V5 setting changes that seems less like real history and more like a Professional Wrestling storyline. I expect we'll find out Vince McMahon is the cunning Lasombra elder manipulator who managed all of this. Maybe in five months he'll turn heel again.<br /> <br /> If you wanted more Lasombra in the Camarilla, a much more elegant solution would simply show the Lasombra AT were much more prevalent in the sect, and that Sabbat claims to have almost wiped them out was hyperbole. And if you wanted the Lasombra AT to be more prominent than the Sabbat Lasombra, you can easily do that with the other changes in V5. Have the Sabbat Lasombra take serious losses in the various failed Crusades and Beckoning so much that the Lasombra AT can say it's them who really represent the clan. Then achieve some kind of spectacular coup against a prominent Sabbat Lasombra that has a major territory be retaken by the Camarilla. As a result, the Lasombra successfully petition the Inner Circle that the Lasombra join the sect and achieve a position on the Inner Circle with its own Justicar (probably with more behind the scenes politics that show the Lasombra AT buildind favors and boons to get it over many centuries). Of course, the Sabbat Lasombra - despite their losses - find this ridiculous and it enrages them. But it'd be up to individual STs to decide which faction &quot;truly&quot; represent the clan and which &quot;deserves&quot; the name of anti-tribu.<br /> <br /> That would get you the end result of more prominent Lasombra in the Camarilla, yet have it be more in line with the previous lore and not require ridiculous things like mass defections of vampires who have huge amounts of Viniculum with the rest of the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:05:03-07:00","id":1417660,"title":"","content":"I've felt there was enough Antitribu for players to play Lasombra in prior editions. <br /> <br /> I don't like the Camarilla getting the Sabbat's religiosity. It could happen, certainly; Sabbat defectors would push for that kind of thing, but It feels like the writers are struggling between wanting to be 'relevant' and projecting their own political experiences onto vampires where it isn't entirely appropriate: The Anarchs are morally grey, the Camarilla as &quot;The Man&quot; are black, and the Sabbat are gone because &quot;we didn't need something blacker than black or it'd make our point silly as the Camarilla would look like the moderates again... hmm&quot; or something to that effect. <br /> <br /> If the metaplot doesn't have the Sabbat come back in a grand, glorious crusade and the 'gehenna war' was made to be part of some -actually good- plan, it will forever keep much of the fanbase playing v20 (but then there's.. let's not get into that) <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dunno, I think the Lasombra are willing to play the long game </div> </div> </div>Lasombra don't lose to ventrue because they're an inferior clan with delusions of grandeur (a lot of them <i>do</i> have delusions of grandeur, but so do Ventrue) The Lasombra lose because they aren't nearly as well organized. They're probably the worst organized clan in the Camarilla, even if we re-include the Brujah (because it's absurd they'd leave) virtually every lasombra wants to be the boss (there's a hilarious flaw in LotB to represent the extremes of that) So I doubt they'd all agree to a master-plan, especially considering the questionable departure from the Sabbat which was surely haphazard at best. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I were writing reasons to make the Lasombra more Camarilla friendly,<s> rather than absolutely fu....</s> I will be using V20 as a jumping off point: <br /> -A few high profile elders and (possibly with a methuselah or two) build up their strengths, encourage faction conflicts, and slaughter their probable opposition to declare a number of high profile cities Camarilla domains. To bolster their cities and add legitimacy to their claims they invite other Camarilla vampires over (A few elders for stability, but also many neonates and thinbloods, struggling with their own cities, come over; they'll be eager meatshields when the counter attack comes) <br /> -The original Lasombra Antitrubu, with news of these new cities taking potential Sabbat attention away from them, start caching in their favours to embrace. <br /> -Gratioano... does something mildly interesting. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:05:58-07:00","id":1417661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417657#post1417657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is one of the V5 setting changes that seems less like real history and more like a Professional Wrestling storyline. I expect we'll find out Vince McMahon is the cunning Lasombra elder manipulator who managed all of this. Maybe in five months he'll turn heel again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, then all of the Lasombra would be fanatically willing to go down with the ship and that makes them all look like a bunch of losers and chumps.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can say, &quot;Completely change the entirety of the story so the Sabbat are not gone&quot; but that's a different argument.<br /> <br /> Here, we get a really good example of how the Lasombra think by them casually betraying their allies of centuries and throwing them under the bus at the first better off they get.<br /> <br /> I think nothing could be more Lasombra than illustrating none of them ever had any loyalty to the sect they founded save what it could do for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lasombra don't lose to ventrue because they're an inferior clan with delusions of grandeur (a lot of them <i>do</i> have delusions of grandeur, but so do Ventrue) The Lasombra lose because they aren't nearly as well organized. They're probably the worst organized clan in the Camarilla, even if we re-include the Brujah (because it's absurd they'd leave) virtually every lasombra wants to be the boss (there's a hilarious flaw in LotB to represent the extremes of that) So I doubt they'd all agree to a master-plan, especially considering the questionable departure from the Sabbat which was surely haphazard at best. </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra literally have their own board of murder justification in the Amis Noctis. They're far from the least organized clan. Yes, they all want to be the boss but that's because they're the ultimate &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; types (and they're wrong because that's the Gangrel) but they are all about making sure the weak are culled from their ranks.<br /> <br /> I personally give them better odds against the Ventrue than the Ventrue against them and note they've never &quot;lost.&quot;<br /> <br /> They've abandoned poor allies for new ones. Yes, the Ventrue think they have the Lasombra's number but their requirements show how ignorant they are:<br /> <br /> * <b>All Lasombra must be Blood Bound</b>: Except the Lasombra have a cure for the Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> * <b>All Lasombra defectors must supply a Sabbat Elder</b>: The Lasombra were going to have to kill a bunch of Sabbat on their way out anyway.<br /> <br /> * <b>All Lasombra are forbidden from having title for sixty years</b>: The Lasombra can build their own power bases without the titles. We already have a Lasombra Primogen in New York City too.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra are used to ridiculous rules they have to work around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2020, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T12:36:52-07:00","id":1417681,"title":"","content":"'shows how ignorant they are' <br /> <br /> Yeah, nah. Fearing the Sabbat for their ability to break blood bonds has been a Camarilla staple. I think V5 works on the premise that the Vauldrie does not exist; it'd explain both the defection and the assumption that they can just blood bond the Lasombra. <br /> <br /> As pointed out, this feels more like pro-wrestling than something you could read in a (vampire) history book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T12:46:56-07:00","id":1417684,"title":"","content":"I like the Lasombra as a clan and I think their defection to the Camarilla makes a lot of sense. I also think the Sabbat are not gone for good and at least half the Lasombra are still active in its ranks. Hopefully I\u2019m right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T13:00:04-07:00","id":1417687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417643#post1417643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4-The Clan curse and oblivion. You'd think this would be a seperate matter, but I think it's indicative of how the writers see lasombra; They don't like lasombra. They want to punish people who like lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I hate those bloody Keepers and Magisters. You're lucky I didn't make them afraid of the dark as well. <br /> <br /> In seriousness, this is an interesting discussion, but I would urge people to credit the writers and developers with at least a modicum of sense, and keep in mind the metaplot is in part designed with the long game in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T13:01:42-07:00","id":1417688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, nah. Fearing the Sabbat for their ability to break blood bonds has been a Camarilla staple. I think V5 works on the premise that the Vauldrie does not exist; it'd explain both the defection and the assumption that they can just blood bond the Lasombra. </div> </div> </div>Ok, but the rules for Lasombra joining Camarilla were thought on the fly by Jackson. Yes, he's Lodin childe and all that, but he doesn't know jack-poo about Occult. He's just obsessed with making Chicago the most important Cam city, because he's the Prince. He hadn't even asked anyone about what should be done with the Lasombra Treaty. He just did it on his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T13:08:33-07:00","id":1417689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417643#post1417643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4-The Clan curse and oblivion. You'd think this would be a seperate matter, but I think it's indicative of how the writers see lasombra; They don't like lasombra. They want to punish people who like lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, can we stop pretending, it's only a weakness?<br /> Lasombra have basically the power to interfere with any kind of technology. Yes, that means they can't use most of it, at least not by themselves, but it also means that they can interfere with something used against them, which was shown in the &quot;Cults...&quot; manuscript.<br /> You can't bug Lasombra, you can't use cameras against Lasombra. The Second Inquisition can do nothing against Lasombra if they won't fight them in the field. And Lasombra are smart enough to know that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":26438,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","user":"TheDreamApologist","date":". 10-11-2020, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T14:44:52-07:00","id":1417710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheDreamApologist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417688#post1417688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He hadn't even asked anyone about what should be done with the Lasombra Treaty. He just did it on his own.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that arrangement only applies to his city, to Chicago. Other Camarilla cities, with other Princes, might well have different requirements for admitting Lasombra or might reject them all together. So, a Lasombra might become a member of the Primogen in New York, because that city has a different arrangement and set of rules - which do not prevent a Lasombra from gaining a title.<br /> <br /> My take on these things is always Doyleist before Watsonian, or out of character before in-character. Admitting some of the Lasombra to the Camarilla serve to shake up the status quo, turn the current situation of the Sabbat into a mystery (which both makes it compelling and give writers room to create) and allows the Lasombra to be a player character clan. In character it makes sense to me as well. Lasombra are highly competitive, to the point of being a <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CompetitionFreak\" target=\"_blank\">Competition Freak</a>. But they also do not like to lose and will not die for an cause, other than their own continued success and existence. The Gehenna War turned into a hideous failure on several levels - and rather than deal with that defeat and likely final death, some of them just went to the Camarilla. It's one step back, two steps forwards, and they can (and will) wait to play their highly competitive games in the Ivory Tower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T14:53:57-07:00","id":1417711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417710#post1417710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My understanding is that arrangement only applies to his city, to Chicago. Other Camarilla cities, with other Princes, might well have different requirements for admitting Lasombra or might reject them all together. So, a Lasombra might become a member of the Primogen in New York, because that city has a different arrangement and set of rules - which do not prevent a Lasombra from gaining a title.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Jackson was suckered on several levels.<br /> <br /> 1. He thought he was accepting a couple of Lasombra refugees, not creating an open door policy for Lasombra.<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;Kevin Jackson made this policy&quot; gives Lasombra in other cities a negotiating precedent.<br /> <br /> 3. The &quot;stake another Sabbat Elder on the way out&quot; makes even warhawks against the Sabbat like, say, Karsh think it's a good idea. It hurts their enemies badly.<br /> <br /> 4. Kevin made the vote one of the Primogen rather than his own decision and, unwittingly, made it so that it was the &quot;will of the city.&quot; Marcel just passed the buck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T15:25:32-07:00","id":1417717,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point that this was really well written thing.<br /> <br /> Kevin Jackson, new, young Prince of Chicago. Childe of Lodin. Leader of one of the most important Camarilla cities. Was outsmarted by someone with much less experience in unlife, just because he was so keen on being the Camarilla poster-child of making difference, by accepting the biggest Ventrue enemies in the vampire world into his turf.<br /> <br /> Should he know better than that? Absolutely.<br /> But that's what you got for not keeping someone older, or at least more knowledgeable in occult, or Sabbat at your hand to ask them needed questions.<br /> <br /> Was that in-character?<br /> Well, aren't Ventrue ridiculed by other for always wanting to chew more than they could fit on their plate?<br /> <br /> And as for the Primogen vote. If Jackson knew it wouldn't end up in a stalemate, he wouldn't ask for it. IMHO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T15:48:18-07:00","id":1417720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheDreamApologist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417717#post1417717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to point that this was really well written thing.<br /> <br /> Kevin Jackson, new, young Prince of Chicago. Childe of Lodin. Leader of one of the most important Camarilla cities. Was outsmarted by someone with much less experience in unlife, just because he was so keen on being the Camarilla poster-child of making difference, by accepting the biggest Ventrue enemies in the vampire world into his turf.<br /> <br /> Should he know better than that? Absolutely.<br /> But that's what you got for not keeping someone older, or at least more knowledgeable in occult, or Sabbat at your hand to ask them needed questions.<br /> <br /> Was that in-character?<br /> Well, aren't Ventrue ridiculed by other for always wanting to chew more than they could fit on their plate?<br /> <br /> And as for the Primogen vote. If Jackson knew it wouldn't end up in a stalemate, he wouldn't ask for it. IMHO</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you have to ask:<br /> <br /> 1. Did Marcel intend for it to go this way? Was the Ministry member just knowing he didn't want to be the name on the &quot;historic&quot; decision.<br /> 2. Was Helena actually the one pulling the strings? Does she benefit from playing politics at an international level or is she just seeing how this amuses her?<br /> <br /> It was a beautiful piece of political writing that let the player characters play a role. Would the Lasombra eventually get in the Camarilla? Probably, but it'd be a delay of a year or two and probably a lot more would be dead in the meantime from the Civil War that's going to happen anyway.<br /> <br /> Kudos to Klara Herb\u00f8l.<br /> <br /> When we played the Sacrifice, EVERYONE supported the Lasombra joining, and that was because they were Anarchs and felt they were going to fuck the Camarilla up from the inside.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2020, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T16:06:19-07:00","id":1417724,"title":"","content":"I wonder how many Lasombra will be actually left in the Sabbat when the dust settles as I don't see the defecting clan loyalists being the type to leave enemies behind them on the way out. Plus if you take into account any potential purge of the remaining Lasombra by the antribu who never really liked the Lasombra much anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24792-vashna","name":"Vashna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T16:24:37-07:00","id":1417729,"title":"","content":"I appreciate that V5 really shook up the status quo, but naturally, I don't like all of the specifics about it. I loved the Sabbat and Sabbat campaigns, and that I can't run such campaigns any longer is something that really puts me off V5. (well, okay, I -can-, but the game certainly doesn't help me). In particular, I think the Sabbat had a much more interesting political structure and more compelling internal conflicts than the Anarchs and the Camarilla (see my thread &quot;Why the Sabbat is more interesting than the Camarilla&quot; for more on this), and my greatest fear about V5 is that it may have squandered much of what made the Sabbat so fascinating.<br /> <br /> I'm not too fond of the Lasombra joining the Camarilla in V5. My main issue is however not on a worldbuilding level, but a purely thematic one - The Lasombra are simply too similar to the Ventrue. They were always, to my mind, a darker version of Ventrue, with very, -very- similar themes. However, that's not to say that the Lasombra necessary had to be in the Sabbat, as Sabbat Ventrue were also a compelling faction, and the story of how they split from the Camarilla Ventrue is very great. But Lasombra and classic Camarilla Ventrue in the same faction feels...boring and bland. I think the Tremere, having the same classy feel as the Ventrue yet being in many ways different, were a better thematic fit as the main rivals of the Ventrue within the Camarilla, and by crippling the Tremere, V5 really damaged this intresting conflict. Had the Lasombra joined the Anarchs instead, I would have had much less issue with it. They could easily have become the Ventrue of the Anarch movement. It would suit both their concept and their lore. Having them stay in the Sabbat would have been fine too.<br /> <br /> However, with roleplaying games, one can always take inspiration from ideas and make something else out of them, so perhaps ironically, my first V5 chronicle actually features the Lasombra joining the Camarilla. But I did it in a different way. I 've written about it in other threads already, but the short form of it is that Lasombra elders don't feel The Beckoning (presumably because they did indeed destroy their antediluvian long ago). With the Sabbat in chaos for many reasons, most of the Amici Noctis lost faith in the Sabbat. In my chronicle the Amici Noctis is a very small group (as I wanted to feature them in scenes in a practical way), and the only one who disagreed was cardinal Menuven. He (they/it) remained in the Sabbat and eventually became its leader in the New World, but the Amici Noctis threw him out and embarked on their new plan.They had decided to try and worm their way into the Camarilla, for they hoped that their many unbeckoned elders would eventually (in a hundred years or so) gain them a high position in that sect. Of course, this plan hinges completely on them managing to hide their beckoning immunity, so the Amici Noctis had to murder tons of noncompliant or untrustworthy Lasombra, but the complicated situation in Mexico City (Sabbat civil war, Gehenna War, Camarilla siege, etc) gave them a good excuse. One of the Amici Noctis, Eleiser de Polanco, led a fraction of Lasombra in Mexico City in defecting to the Camarilla, and handed the Camarilla tons of Sabbat secrets - and scores of dead Lasombra, especially followers of the Path of Night. Naturally, the Camarilla weren't about to trust a traitor, but the situation on the ground in Mexico City was very, very complicated, and de Polanco made them an offer they couldn't refuse. So, controversially, Fiorenza di Savona of clan Ventrue made a deal with the devil - de Polanco would be allowed to rule as Camarilla prince of Mexico City, with her as his seneschal, but the Lasombra would -not- get a justicar, and Polanco had to consent to the Lasombra primogen being a known Camarilla-loyalist from a long Lasombra antitribu lineage. De Polanco also had to purge all known path of Night followers and overt Abyss mysticists from the Lasombras ranks, but that wasn't a big hindrance - most of those had left for the Gehenna War or escaped with vice regent Menuven to Acapulco.<br /> <br /> TLDR; in my chronicle, the Lasombra did join the Camarilla, but as a very long-term power play, rather than from desperation. The Camarilla accepted this with reluctance, but it happened thanks to a unilateral action on a local level in Mexico City, that was only approved by the Inner Circle after the fact, because they couldn't say no to being handed Mexico City on a plate. And some really metal Lasombra like Menuven remains staunch Sabbat loyalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 10-11-2020, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T16:36:34-07:00","id":1417731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the Lasombra joining the Camarilla is one of the less good ideas in V5. My main issue is however not on a worldbuilding level, but a purely thematic one - The Lasombra are simply too similar to the Ventrue. They were always, to my mind, a darker version of Ventrue, with very, -very- similar themes. I think the Tremere, having the same classy feel as the Ventrue yet being in many ways different, were a better thematic fit as the main rivals of the Ventrue within the Camarilla, and by crippling the Tremere, V5 really damaged this conflict. Had the Lasombra joined the Anarchs instead, I would have had much less issue with it. They could easily have become the Ventrue of the Anarch movement. It would suit both their concept and their lore. </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, I feel differently on this.<br /> <br /> My thoughts being:<br /> <br /> 1. The Ventrue and Lasombra make excellent rivals in the sect and there's now a Shadow Lords vs. Silver Fangs power struggle going on between them. The Lasombra offer an alternative to the stodgy old power structure that previously existed.<br /> <br /> 2. The Ventrue have never had anything but glowing support from the Tremere because the former have needed the latter and vice versa. The Tremere don't WANT Princes and Praxises (though they won't turn them down if they fall into their lap) but need stability that the Ventrue provide in spades. Their current crappy situation shows the Ventrue are vulnerable without their &quot;Court Wizards&quot; but also that the Ventrue did jack for the Tremere when they needed them.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Tremere as Ventrue rivals is a thing I've never done so that may explain why the Lasombra fill a void in my world where they don't in yours.<br /> <br /> 3. The Lasombra really were wasted in the Sabbat where they were just the Ventrue of the sect. The Tzimisce served the same role as the Tremere to the Ventrue and it was really an unnecessary duplication. It doesn't help the Sabbat don't have any of the culture and politicking that the Camarilla does. No need to be subtle in the Sabbat if you can just challenge a rival to monomancy like you're Klingons.<br /> <br /> 4. I feel like the Ventrue don't have nearly the same amount of flavor or panache as the Lasombra. They're kind of bland compared to the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Cool story, FYI!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T19:48:07-07:00","id":1417755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417731#post1417731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ultimately, I feel differently on this.<br /> <br /> My thoughts being:<br /> <br /> 1. The Ventrue and Lasombra make excellent rivals in the sect and there's now a Shadow Lords vs. Silver Fangs power struggle going on between them. The Lasombra offer an alternative to the stodgy old power structure that previously existed.<br /> <br /> 2. The Ventrue have never had anything but glowing support from the Tremere because the former have needed the latter and vice versa. The Tremere don't WANT Princes and Praxises (though they won't turn them down if they fall into their lap) but need stability that the Ventrue provide in spades. Their current crappy situation shows the Ventrue are vulnerable without their &amp;quot;Court Wizards&amp;quot; but also that the Ventrue did jack for the Tremere when they needed them.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Tremere as Ventrue rivals is a thing I've never done so that may explain why the Lasombra fill a void in my world where they don't in yours.<br /> <br /> 3. The Lasombra really were wasted in the Sabbat where they were just the Ventrue of the sect. The Tzimisce served the same role as the Tremere to the Ventrue and it was really an unnecessary duplication. It doesn't help the Sabbat don't have any of the culture and politicking that the Camarilla does. No need to be subtle in the Sabbat if you can just challenge a rival to monomancy like you're Klingons.<br /> <br /> 4. I feel like the Ventrue don't have nearly the same amount of flavor or panache as the Lasombra. They're kind of bland compared to the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Cool story, FYI!</div> </div> </div> </div>I like both the Ventrue and the Lasombra, but I feel they fill different niches. Ventrue are the aristocracy, Lasombra are the kingmakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T20:42:39-07:00","id":1417761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417755#post1417755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like both the Ventrue and the Lasombra, but I feel they fill different niches. Ventrue are the aristocracy, Lasombra are the kingmakers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that, for some reason, the Lasombra in 5th Edition are back to trying to control the church. It's a fertile ground for people who want to control televangelists and megachurches.<br /> <br /> Places which talk a great deal about God but are only opiates of the masses controlled by those who don't believe.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set could also do it but, bluntly, are a bit too sincerely religious to properly handle those guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T20:46:35-07:00","id":1417762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417755#post1417755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like both the Ventrue and the Lasombra, but I feel they fill different niches. Ventrue are the aristocracy, Lasombra are the kingmakers.</div> </div> </div> </div>wait now, shouldn't it be the other way around?<br /> <br /> I mean, to my understanding, the Ventrue had a great split between old nobility and the new burgher class during the late middle ages, and the old nobility faction became the Ventrue antitribu of the Sabbat. Therefore, most of the Camarilla Ventrue are rather descended from capitalists and burghers, and their culture is as focused on business and money as on nobility and tradition.<br /> <br /> The core of the Lasombra, on the other hand, mostly come from backgrounds as Spanish nobility and the more or less feudal upper class of Latin American colonial caste systems - shouldn't they hold aristocratic identity in even higher regard than the Ventrue does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T20:50:27-07:00","id":1417763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417761#post1417761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that, for some reason, the Lasombra in 5th Edition are back to trying to control the church. It's a fertile ground for people who want to control televangelists and megachurches.<br /> <br /> Places which talk a great deal about God but are only opiates of the masses controlled by those who don't believe.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set could also do it but, bluntly, are a bit too sincerely religious to properly handle those guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that super-weird. Wouldn't it make much more sense to stay REALLY FAR AWAY from the church now that the Second Inquisition knows about vampires and is actively trying to eradicate them?<br /> <br /> My favorite church vampires are actually the Brujah. The evangelist Brujah coterie in Clanbook: Brujah was a fantastic concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T20:53:37-07:00","id":1417765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417762#post1417762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> wait now, shouldn't it be the other way around?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it?<br /> <br /> Canonically, the Lasombra don't believe in aristocracy. The Lasombra believe that even the lowliest peasant can rise up to the highest ranks in the Clan if they're badass or cunning enough. This was actually a progressive attitude in the Middle Ages and partially why they leaned toward dealing with the church. While it rarely worked out that way, nothing particularly prevented a peasant born clergyman from rising to be Pope since Peter was a fisherman rather than a nobleman.<br /> <br /> In the Sabbat, they became the Clan of Ayn Rand meets X-men's Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> So some Lasombra are aristocrats but they're very much of the &quot;self made man&quot; belief and that if they are arsitocrats, they're from the kind who EMBODY it.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue, by contrast, had the view that some people were &quot;born better&quot; and normally took from the military aristocracy of the world and considered peasants as well as Low Clans to be beneath them. The current shift toward merchants and businessmen was something that happened in part because so many of their ancient Houses and bloodlines were annihilated by the Inquisition and they underwent (what they would consider) a degeneration the same way the Brujah went from being the Clan of Socrates to the Clan of Sex Pistols.<br /> <br /> Even now they tend to have heavy classicist tones and probably a racial one if you look hard enough.<br /> <br /> I'd argue the Ventrue are closer to how the Tzimisce view things but the Tzimisce figured out how to MAKE themselves better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417763#post1417763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find that super-weird. Wouldn't it make much more sense to stay REALLY FAR AWAY from the church now that the Second Inquisition knows about vampires and is actively trying to eradicate them?<br /> <br /> My favorite church vampires are actually the Brujah. The evangelist Brujah coterie in Clanbook: Brujah was a fantastic concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lasombra would argue that taking over the church would be the best way to safeguard yourself.<br /> <br /> However, that is LITERALLY what caused the first Inquisition alongside Goratrix trying to steal the Ark of the Covenant.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not making that last part up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2020, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T00:57:29-07:00","id":1417780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417687#post1417687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I hate those bloody Keepers and Magisters. You're lucky I didn't make them afraid of the dark as well.<br /> <br /> In seriousness, this is an interesting discussion, but I would urge people to credit the writers and developers with at least a modicum of sense, and keep in mind the metaplot is in part designed with the long game in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I look at the metaplot, and yeah, I can see lots of potential there. The issue is -right now-. Taking all the cool stuff away for a number of years for a big reveal leaves us dry and hanging -right now-. Meanwhile the vagueness of &quot;these things that happened between revised and 2009&quot; might be there to build up mystery, but have you also considered it just looks vague and gives the impression that the writers are just making big sweeping changes with vagueness because they hadn't really thought too much about how they wanted to do something, they just wanted something done. I see a lot of potential, but I see a lot of potential for disaster, and it seems clear to me that you could have avoided all this had the metaplot moved with the present rather than something done retroactively. 'Things now' are bad. So 'things later', presumably being writen by the same people who chose to make 'things now' bad, causes concern. <br /> <br /> As to my comments about Lasombra. <br /> No, I don't believe you hate lasombra (Did you write their section in LotC? That was solid). But V5 was written by a team, and have you noticed that there's a huge disrepency between the mechanics of the game and the story now? Elders and Ancients are supposedly scary, but they're subject to the same five-level limitation as high gens and ordinary mortals. Thin bloods are no longer -between a vampire and a ghoul- but rather lost such powers so they can become absurd apothocaries. For the Lasombra: Dominate has gained numerous new restrictions and is weaker, Potence is now a strange collection of absurdly specific strength-based gimicks rather than a simple strength enhancer and no longer fits the old image of the clan, Obtenebration has given up it's identity to be a necromancy bastard and the shadow powers it once had are weak and laughable... Yeah, I think you can forgive me for believing some people on the staff do not like Lasombra. Sure I can justify playing them more in V5 with their escape from the Sabbat, but why would I want to play them in the first place? They are weak whilst their culture has always been -we are not weak- . Not to mention I can't play with paths as they don't exist, and Abyss mystics can't exist because using Oblivion that much would mechanically drain you of your humanity. <br /> <br /> So things right now look bad. Saying 'oh, we're long term planners and things are coming in the future...' Yeah, nah, no thanks. The mechanics work against the fluff; your team is literally working against itself. And then there's the times where the new fluff is working with the mechanics and... It's not an isolated incident. We could be having the same discussion about the Tremere: The fluff has potential to un-fuck itself and be a grand master-stroke of writing, yet we shouldn't speculate for the future when things are fucked -right now-. Also Thaumaturgy has been mechanically re-written to... not be thaumaturgy? And they also have Dominate but it now sucks... and they can't blood bond... so they should be getting murdered by their ghouls or something. <br /> <br /> I can credit some of you with sense, but 'the long game in mind' shouldn't mean that the here and now should suffer like so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T04:01:17-07:00","id":1417789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I look at the metaplot, and yeah, I can see lots of potential there. The issue is -right now-. Taking all the cool stuff away for a number of years for a big reveal leaves us dry and hanging -right now-.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Engage with any game, media, whatever, and you will rarely find immediate gratification. It is our job, in part, to keep our customers engaged. So your requirement for everything to be given to you <b>right now</b> is something you are unlikely to have satisfied. <i>Your </i>issue is <b>right now</b>. The solution is patience and invention. If the toy you want to play with is scheduled for release in a year's time, create a variation on an existing one, or play with a Toreador instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile the vagueness of &quot;these things that happened between revised and 2009&quot; might be there to build up mystery, but have you also considered it just looks vague and gives the impression that the writers are just making big sweeping changes with vagueness because they hadn't really thought too much about how they wanted to do something, they just wanted something done.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Vagueness is a deliberate choice, as fans react poorly to grand sweeping changes such as the Ravnos being annihilated, and Storytellers should be given room to make the game what they see fit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see a lot of potential, but I see a lot of potential for disaster, and it seems clear to me that you could have avoided all this had the metaplot moved with the present rather than something done retroactively. 'Things now' are bad. So 'things later', presumably being writen by the same people who chose to make 'things now' bad, causes concern.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever we set the changes, there will be some folks unhappy with them. The excellent news with this RPG, and others, is you can adjust dates and events to fit your group. We will never tell you you're doing it wrong. If we release a book that changes the setting <b>now </b>some people playing Halruaans while reading that book might think &quot;well I don't want to be caught in the middle of a Spellplague!&quot; while making the change historically might make them say &quot;I don't want the Spellplague in my past!&quot; Your opinion is valid, but your desire to be satisfied comes at the cost of the desires of others, just as theirs comes at yours. Ipso facto, metaplot always does this and we just have to run for our groups in the best way we can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As to my comments about Lasombra.<br /> No, I don't believe you hate lasombra (Did you write their section in LotC? That was solid).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I did not. That bastard Eddy Webb didn't hire me for Lore of the Clans. However, I did write every clan for V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But V5 was written by a team, and have you noticed that there's a huge disrepency between the mechanics of the game and the story now? Elders and Ancients are supposedly scary, but they're subject to the same five-level limitation as high gens and ordinary mortals. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I see this complaint occasionally, and am always surprised at how many people seem to have missed the Generation and Blood Potency table, have high gens and ordinary mortals with multiple dice pools valued at eight or higher, have neonates with five or six Disciplines rated at 4 or 5, have fledglings influencing global institutions and political structures, and thin-bloods Blood Bonding lots of younger Generation vampires. Now, obviously, none of that is happening, but several fans really seem hung up on the idea that because a number doesn't go above five it automatically weakens the character, when in fact there's a raft of reasons for an elder to be scarier than a neonate. Plus, very few level 6+ Disciplines were workable in a game based around social conflict and operating with subtlety. If you want your vampire to create earthquakes, that's fine, but I'd be hard-pressed to play the story where they do that more than once before they're destroyed by every other vampire in the domain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thin bloods are no longer -between a vampire and a ghoul- but rather lost such powers so they can become absurd apothocaries.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thin-Blood Alchemy is there to demonstrate the changeable nature of vitae, mutations in the Blood, and their status as a kind of evolution of Kindred. They can literally change the nature of vitae because they're a step beyond regular vampires. However, if you don't like it, just deny your players the Merit they have to take to access it. It's not an obligatory part of every thin-blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Lasombra: Dominate has gained numerous new restrictions and is weaker, Potence is now a strange collection of absurdly specific strength-based gimicks rather than a simple strength enhancer and no longer fits the old image of the clan, Obtenebration has given up it's identity to be a necromancy bastard and the shadow powers it once had are weak and laughable... <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is subjective, as I find Dominate and Potence infinitely more interesting now. Dominate doesn't just crash every mystery plot and Potence isn't just a damage sim. Plus, how many big bruiser Lasombra were ever depicted in previous editions? As for Obtenebration / Oblivion, by connecting Oblivion, the Abyss, and the Underworld, we help unify the World of Darkness' cosmology in a way that makes sense. The Abyss is a place of nothingness. Oblivion is a place of nothingness. And yes, Oblivion should have shadow powers because it makes a hell of a lot more sense thematically for vampires to manipulate shadows rather than thick black tentacles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I think you can forgive me for believing some people on the staff do not like Lasombra. Sure I can justify playing them more in V5 with their escape from the Sabbat, but why would I want to play them in the first place? They are weak whilst their culture has always been -we are not weak- . Not to mention I can't play with paths as they don't exist, and Abyss mystics can't exist because using Oblivion that much would mechanically drain you of your humanity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You may want to play them because characters don't have to be over-powered to be interesting, and rather, faults and nuance make for interesting characters. The Lasombra aren't weak. They're special for their new role, they still access a Discipline very few vampires know about, they have influence in the Church - where most vampires fear to tread - and they're just as ruthless as they've always been. If you want Paths of Enlightenment, pick up a Conviction and help set your Chronicle Tenets. It's really that easy. If you want a moral paragon of an Abyss Mystic, who doesn't lose Humanity while they play with the stuff of entropy, you're talking about such a character contradiction that that character deserves what's coming to them. Abyss Mysticism is close to infernalism in its unholy nature. Of course it drains your Humanity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So things right now look bad. Saying 'oh, we're long term planners and things are coming in the future...' Yeah, nah, no thanks. The mechanics work against the fluff; your team is literally working against itself. And then there's the times where the new fluff is working with the mechanics and... It's not an isolated incident. We could be having the same discussion about the Tremere: The fluff has potential to un-fuck itself and be a grand master-stroke of writing, yet we shouldn't speculate for the future when things are fucked -right now-.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that things are fucked <b>right now</b> due to the number of people playing with this material and enjoying it, but again we come to the problem of <b>right now</b>. I didn't like the Batman franchise when Batman Forever came out, but boy, was my opinion changed with the release of Batman &amp; Robin. Different tastes, and all that. I suggest playing with material you enjoy, and that may well entail going back to a prior edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also Thaumaturgy has been mechanically re-written to... not be thaumaturgy? And they also have Dominate but it now sucks... and they can't blood bond... so they should be getting murdered by their ghouls or something.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy is Blood Sorcery. It's all about the blood. It made very little sense to have all the bloat of previous editions, and Tremere firing lightning bolts wasn't in keeping with the theme of Vampire. And yes, the Tremere are in an extremely precarious position with everyone they'd historically Bonded. However, the book stats right in their Clan Bane section that they can still Blood Bond mortals and create ghouls, so I recommend re-reading that section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can credit some of you with sense<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> but 'the long game in mind'<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417780#post1417780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> shouldn't mean that the here and now should suffer like so.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think to call any of what's going on &quot;suffering&quot; is hyperbolic. While lots of people do seem to enjoy the V5 Lasombra, your opinion is valid and I strongly recommend changing the Lasombra, Tremere, thin-bloods, elders, ancients, Obtenebration / Oblivion, and Thaumaturgy for your game to suit your vision for what they should be, if you've not already done so. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T04:30:39-07:00","id":1417791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417789#post1417789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Engage with any game, media, whatever, and you will rarely find immediate gratification. It is our job, in part, to keep our customers engaged. So your requirement for everything to be given to you <b>right now</b> is something you are unlikely to have satisfied. <i>Your </i>issue is <b>right now</b>. The solution is patience and invention. If the toy you want to play with is scheduled for release in a year's time, create a variation on an existing one, or play with a Toreador instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Vagueness is a deliberate choice, as fans react poorly to grand sweeping changes such as the Ravnos being annihilated, and Storytellers should be given room to make the game what they see fit. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Whenever we set the changes, there will be some folks unhappy with them. The excellent news with this RPG, and others, is you can adjust dates and events to fit your group. We will never tell you you're doing it wrong. If we release a book that changes the setting <b>now </b>some people playing Halruaans while reading that book might think &amp;quot;well I don't want to be caught in the middle of a Spellplague!&amp;quot; while making the change historically might make them say &amp;quot;I don't want the Spellplague in my past!&amp;quot; Your opinion is valid, but your desire to be satisfied comes at the cost of the desires of others, just as theirs comes at yours. Ipso facto, metaplot always does this and we just have to run for our groups in the best way we can.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I did not. That bastard Eddy Webb didn't hire me for Lore of the Clans. However, I did write every clan for V5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I see this complaint occasionally, and am always surprised at how many people seem to have missed the Generation and Blood Potency table, have high gens and ordinary mortals with multiple dice pools valued at eight or higher, have neonates with five or six Disciplines rated at 4 or 5, have fledglings influencing global institutions and political structures, and thin-bloods Blood Bonding lots of younger Generation vampires. Now, obviously, none of that is happening, but several fans really seem hung up on the idea that because a number doesn't go above five it automatically weakens the character, when in fact there's a raft of reasons for an elder to be scarier than a neonate. Plus, very few level 6+ Disciplines were workable in a game based around social conflict and operating with subtlety. If you want your vampire to create earthquakes, that's fine, but I'd be hard-pressed to play the story where they do that more than once before they're destroyed by every other vampire in the domain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thin-Blood Alchemy is there to demonstrate the changeable nature of vitae, mutations in the Blood, and their status as a kind of evolution of Kindred. They can literally change the nature of vitae because they're a step beyond regular vampires. However, if you don't like it, just deny your players the Merit they have to take to access it. It's not an obligatory part of every thin-blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is subjective, as I find Dominate and Potence infinitely more interesting now. Dominate doesn't just crash every mystery plot and Potence isn't just a damage sim. Plus, how many big bruiser Lasombra were ever depicted in previous editions? As for Obtenebration / Oblivion, by connecting Oblivion, the Abyss, and the Underworld, we help unify the World of Darkness' cosmology in a way that makes sense. The Abyss is a place of nothingness. Oblivion is a place of nothingness. And yes, Oblivion should have shadow powers because it makes a hell of a lot more sense thematically for vampires to manipulate shadows rather than thick black tentacles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You may want to play them because characters don't have to be over-powered to be interesting, and rather, faults and nuance make for interesting characters. The Lasombra aren't weak. They're special for their new role, they still access a Discipline very few vampires know about, they have influence in the Church - where most vampires fear to tread - and they're just as ruthless as they've always been. If you want Paths of Enlightenment, pick up a Conviction and help set your Chronicle Tenets. It's really that easy. If you want a moral paragon of an Abyss Mystic, who doesn't lose Humanity while they play with the stuff of entropy, you're talking about such a character contradiction that that character deserves what's coming to them. Abyss Mysticism is close to infernalism in its unholy nature. Of course it drains your Humanity. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree that things are fucked <b>right now</b> due to the number of people playing with this material and enjoying it, but again we come to the problem of <b>right now</b>. I didn't like the Batman franchise when Batman Forever came out, but boy, was my opinion changed with the release of Batman &amp; Robin. Different tastes, and all that. I suggest playing with material you enjoy, and that may well entail going back to a prior edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy is Blood Sorcery. It's all about the blood. It made very little sense to have all the bloat of previous editions, and Tremere firing lightning bolts wasn't in keeping with the theme of Vampire. And yes, the Tremere are in an extremely precarious position with everyone they'd historically Bonded. However, the book stats right in their Clan Bane section that they can still Blood Bond mortals and create ghouls, so I recommend re-reading that section.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why thank you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh no...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think to call any of what's going on &amp;quot;suffering&amp;quot; is hyperbolic. While lots of people do seem to enjoy the V5 Lasombra, your opinion is valid and I strongly recommend changing the Lasombra, Tremere, thin-bloods, elders, ancients, Obtenebration / Oblivion, and Thaumaturgy for your game to suit your vision for what they should be, if you've not already done so. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is an awesome post. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T06:07:57-07:00","id":1417799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417789#post1417789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Engage with any game, media, whatever, and you will rarely find immediate gratification. It is our job, in part, to keep our customers engaged. So your requirement for everything to be given to you <b>right now</b> is something you are unlikely to have satisfied. <i>Your </i>issue is <b>right now</b>. The solution is patience and invention. If the toy you want to play with is scheduled for release in a year's time, create a variation on an existing one, or play with a Toreador instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't insinuate that I and others who disagree with V5's stances are just... Toreador.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vagueness is a deliberate choice, as fans react poorly to grand sweeping changes such as the Ravnos being annihilated, and Storytellers should be given room to make the game what they see fit. </div> </div> </div>And yet, grand sweeping changes like the second largest sect buggering off into the middle east, leaving their cities open to whatever... The Camarilla giving up it's monopoly and a big part of it's identity, the brujah leaving the Camarilla for a contrivance.... not to mention the huge sweeping mechanical changes.<br /> <br /> &quot;fans react poorly to grand sweeping changes&quot; so we did just that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whenever we set the changes, there will be some folks unhappy with them. The excellent news with this RPG, and others, is you can adjust dates and events to fit your group. We will never tell you you're doing it wrong. If we release a book that changes the setting <b>now </b>some people playing Halruaans while reading that book might think &quot;well I don't want to be caught in the middle of a Spellplague!&quot; while making the change historically might make them say &quot;I don't want the Spellplague in my past!&quot; Your opinion is valid, but your desire to be satisfied comes at the cost of the desires of others, just as theirs comes at yours. Ipso facto, metaplot always does this and we just have to run for our groups in the best way we can. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(V5 totally took a political stance and told some players they were playing it wrong. I am not of that political persuasion, but it came off as an unpleasant, It really does tell players they're playing a game wrong)</span><br /> <br /> On the surface that's a fine rationale, but it breaks apart in reality. When everyone's mostly on the same page after reading the same book, with perhaps some different interpretations, that's great. When it becomes the norm for fans to need to justify their changes and establish what they want out of playing a certain clan when the fluff and rules no longer support the vision they had built up. Players and storytellers need to be on the same page and treated fairly. If the Storyteller wants to make changes, say they want to use something from first edition instead of V5, it is a little bit inconvenient for players who actually liked the v5 writeup more and had invested themselves into their character through that (especially if the shuffle comes late) whilst, if I wanted to play a Classic Tremere, steeped in a Hermetic paradigm, who creates all sorts of miracles with his will rather than play NuTremere who's really just a blood bender with some rituals, I'd need to demand concessions from my storyteller, and then I'd be <i>that Guy. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see this complaint occasionally, and am always surprised at how many people seem to have missed the Generation and Blood Potency table, </div> </div> </div>Nope.Let me stop you there: I saw the table. I have not stated anything concerning the power of elders without considering the table. It is not a good table.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thin-Blood Alchemy is there to demonstrate the changeable nature of vitae, mutations in the Blood, and their status as a kind of evolution of Kindred. They can literally change the nature of vitae because they're a step beyond regular vampires. However, if you don't like it, just deny your players the Merit they have to take to access it. It's not an obligatory part of every thin-blood. </div> </div> </div>This is the first time in five editions, not counting for the dark ages, where thin blood is considered 'a step beyond regular vampires'. If we were to consider the subject of alchemy properly, you'd quickly realise they're the result of an incomplete alchemical process: Mortals are lead, Caine is Gold. Mortals are at 0, Caine is a step below God. actual alchemy is deeper than the DnD stuff, and it's a shame thin bloods get this flimsy power to give them a nice happy niche and discourage them from actually joining the Jyhad proper.<br /> as thin bloods do not have access to normal disciplines for some reason in V5, it might as well be obligatory, because there is no alternative to them acquiring magic power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is subjective, as I find Dominate and Potence infinitely more interesting now. Dominate doesn't just crash every mystery plot and Potence isn't just a damage sim. Plus, how many big bruiser Lasombra were ever depicted in previous editions? As for Obtenebration / Oblivion, by connecting Oblivion, the Abyss, and the Underworld, we help unify the World of Darkness' cosmology in a way that makes sense. The Abyss is a place of nothingness. Oblivion is a place of nothingness. And yes, Oblivion should have shadow powers because it makes a hell of a lot more sense thematically for vampires to manipulate shadows rather than thick black tentacles. </div> </div> </div>-If Dominate crushes your mystery plot you'd better come up with better plots. Combine it with obfuscate, or use that -only one Dominate at a time- rule that seems to have been forgotten.<br /> -Potence, as just strength, was elegant in it's intuitive simplicity. It would help you jump, climb, swim, grapple, pounce, throw... V5 potence is absurd. &quot;Do I learn to jump or do I learn to cause lethal damage with my fists? I must keep in mind that being able to jump real high does nothing for kicks or...&quot; like, what?<br /> - not making easy sense preserves the mystery and allows for different branches of occultism to arise; Don't fucking solve our answers for us. How can an abyss mystic be taken seriously when their musings of 'a realm outside of creation' are just answered by 'yo it's this thing at the bottom of the underworld, get off your high horse!' How many characters are you killing by giving easy answers to what should be difficult questions? Plus, and you'll have to bare with me on this one: The Abyss being wraith's Oblivion is just a shit solution. Also it begs the question as to how Giovanni and Lasombra weren't once identical bloodlines because before the feast they had the exact same disciplines... oh yeah, the weakness. You've all really fucked up the occultism factor of this kinda thing, for Lasombra and all the necromancers too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You may want to play them because characters don't have to be over-powered to be interesting, and rather, faults and nuance make for interesting characters. The Lasombra aren't weak. They're special for their new role </div> </div> </div>Hey, I was extremely happy to play Caitiffs and thinbloods before they got their snowflake power that makes them absurdly useful. I fill my dark ages games with an abundanced of nuanced Lasombra, some of my favourites are positively timid. The issue is, in V5, they are absolutely shoe-horned in as fools and whipping boys. Thats their 'new role'. Where before I could play them in any number of ways, now they're a C-list clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree that things are fucked <b>right now</b> due to the number of people playing with this material and enjoying it, but again we come to the problem of <b>right now</b>. I didn't like the Batman franchise when Batman Forever came out, but boy, was my opinion changed with the release of Batman &amp; Robin. Different tastes, and all that. I suggest playing with material you enjoy, and that may well entail going back to a prior edition. </div> </div> </div>It dropped off the RPG best sellers list, did it not? The Prior edition does seem to be holding more steady. (though I'll admit, this is through online sales and V5 has the huge advantage of being in stores)<br /> &quot;going back to a prior edition&quot; is not a great suggestion, marketing wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thaumaturgy is Blood Sorcery. It's all about the blood. It made very little sense to have all the bloat of previous editions, and Tremere firing lightning bolts wasn't in keeping with the theme of Vampire. And yes, the Tremere are in an extremely precarious position with everyone they'd historically Bonded. However, the book stats right in their Clan Bane section that they can still Blood Bond mortals and create ghouls, so I recommend re-reading that section. </div> </div> </div>To the latter- Ok, that's good. Point conceeded.<br /> <br /> To Thaumaturgy: Your assertion is derived from an incomplete understanding of what thaumaturgy is. Thaumaturgy is not 'blood magic' it's miracle working. Vitae is a sacrifice because vampires store their magic juice there. Saying it's gotta be 'blood themed magic' is like saying nuclear power should only be used to power nuclear technologies: behold my uranium lightbulb.<br /> Nah seriously, Did you think when people wrote the first edition the people who made Tremere a bunch of Western-tradition Hermetic mages were somehow misguided in adding multiple paths, paths like the lure of flames, and that they didn't know what they were talking about and should've kept everything blood-themed with maybe some curses mixed in? That sounds positively juvenile.<span style=\"font-size:8px\"> Also have you read Mage: The Ascension by any chance? </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think to call any of what's going on &quot;suffering&quot; is hyperbolic. While lots of people do seem to enjoy the V5 Lasombra, your opinion is valid and I strongly recommend changing the Lasombra, Tremere, thin-bloods, elders, ancients, Obtenebration / Oblivion, and Thaumaturgy for your game to suit your vision for what they should be, if you've not already done so. </div> </div> </div>Much of the people who seem to be enjoying this edition's Lasombra seem to be the people who did not enjoy the Lasombra in the last one. I've seen nothing but anguish concerning Oblivion. Many are still upset the Sabbat are gone. The point of praise seems to be the new weakness: The old weakness seemed like 'not a problem' till you really thought about it, and thus this praise is not from people who 'really thought about it' (and thus played the clan)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-12-2020, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T06:11:08-07:00","id":1417801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417765#post1417765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lasombra would argue that taking over the church would be the best way to safeguard yourself.<br /> <br /> However, that is LITERALLY what caused the first Inquisition alongside Goratrix trying to steal the Ark of the Covenant.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not making that last part up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the rest of your points, but I don't understand this one. Why would they try to influence the church if it already backfired terribly once? Wouldn't it seem even more likely to do so today? I just can't wrap my head around the Lasombra-church theme, it worked fine in Vampire the Dark Ages, but it feels so forced in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T06:28:19-07:00","id":1417802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417801#post1417801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the rest of your points, but I don't understand this one. Why would they try to influence the church if it already backfired terribly once? Wouldn't it seem even more likely to do so today? I just can't wrap my head around the Lasombra-church theme, it worked fine in Vampire the Dark Ages, but it feels so forced in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>In simple terms, the Lasombra seek power where others fear to tread. The Church (and Protestant offshoots) may not be as influential as it was in 1299 but it's still an immense resource of political power, financial power, and social power that leaving alone is going to be potentially deadly. Also, the Lasombra are the kind of people who would tell you that if you get yourself killed doing something then it was your own fault for being weak rather than than it was innately a bad idea in the first place (even if this is a somewhat insane philosophy).<br /> <br /> My general assumption is that Lasombra in the Church also are some of the WORST people and that they will undermine any sort of genuine faith or good will that a religious institution has. They're the people who will raise up people like Reverend Bakker and Falwell as well as make the primary goal to &quot;Give money for God's blessings&quot; and &quot;Hate on X group because it will help you.&quot; Vampire hunting is something that they will undermine because faith struggles to survive in such an environment and the actual spiritual conflict between good vs. evil doesn't mean much.<br /> <br /> And if you have really brass balls, Lasombra might be willing to try to direct church-based hunters against their enemies.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, like most humans, Lasombra never learn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And yet, grand sweeping changes like the second largest sect buggering off into the middle east, leaving their cities open to whatever... The Camarilla giving up it's monopoly and a big part of it's identity, the brujah leaving the Camarilla for a contrivance.... not to mention the huge sweeping mechanical changes.<br /> <br /> &quot;fans react poorly to grand sweeping changes&quot; so we did just that...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla has always been hypocritical about its monopoly as we see with the fact the Giovanni were forbidden from joining the sect and participating in any way. The Brujah membership in the sect had also been the subject of numerous rebellions from the Treaty of Thorns onward with the French Revolution, Brujah Council, California revolt, and Council Wars being just some of them. The killing of Hardelstadt was just the final straw and honestly was probably better for the organization as a whole.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs were an existential threat to the Camarilla and still are. Keeping them inside was lunacy.<br /> <br /> Mind you, part of this is due to the &quot;at my table&quot; phenomenon as at some people's table, I have unironically heard, &quot;The Brujah are the loyal opposition.&quot;<br /> <br /> My response was, &quot;In what universe have the Brujah ever been LOYAL?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hey, I was extremely happy to play Caitiffs and thinbloods before they got their snowflake power that makes them absurdly useful.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't call them that. Disagreeing with the modern game or preferring older editions is fine. Trashing them is not on the forums that support said game are not. Only warning.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah seriously, Did you think when people wrote the first edition the people who made Tremere a bunch of Western-tradition Hermetic mages were somehow misguided in adding multiple paths, paths like the lure of flames, and that they didn't know what they were talking about and should've kept everything blood-themed with maybe some curses mixed in? That sounds positively juvenile.<span style=\"font-size:8px\"> Also have you read Mage: The Ascension by any chance? </span></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a good argument that a lot of Disciplines were unbalanced with Thaumaturgy being &quot;The One Discipline to Rule them All&quot; with Paths being Micro-Disciplines. Getting rid of Thaumaturgy Paths and replacing them with one-shot rituals preprepared restored a lot of balance to it. There's also been a lot of changes to the crunch that makes other Disciplines more attractive. Potence, Fortitude, and Celerity were very useful but also very boring. Animalism now actually has a purpose with the fact you can drink Animal Blood with it. Serpentis is no longer the worst Discipline in the setting.<br /> <br /> I loved the old system but tweaking it was not a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much of the people who seem to be enjoying this edition's Lasombra seem to be the people who did not enjoy the Lasombra in the last one. I've seen nothing but anguish concerning Oblivion. Many are still upset the Sabbat are gone. The point of praise seems to be the new weakness: The old weakness seemed like 'not a problem' till you really thought about it, and thus this praise is not from people who 'really thought about it' (and thus played the clan)</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't make these kind of assumptions. My ten year game set in Tampa, Florida was about it being set in &quot;The only Lasombra Antitribu-run city in North America.&quot; Almost all of the players there were Lasombra fanatics and all of them have responded incredibly well to the new Lasombra changes. &quot;The Sacrifice&quot; was our most popular game ever and led to some heated but fun conversations and everyone is responding well to the addition of ghosts in the Lasombra power spread. Mind you, I should note that the Abyss has ALWAYS been the Underworld in our game so it's not exactly a big leap either.<br /> <br /> Lots of people made that leap in previous games.<br /> <br /> As for the weakness, it's been incorporated fine. I admit, though, we did it because we stated SOMETHING is stirring in the abyss and ramping up Lasombra weirdness incredibly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It dropped off the RPG best sellers list, did it not? The Prior edition does seem to be holding more steady. (though I'll admit, this is through online sales and V5 has the huge advantage of being in stores) &quot;going back to a prior edition&quot; is not a great suggestion, marketing wise.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This forum is not going to have the, &quot;I don't like <i>Star Trek: Discovery</i> or <i>The Force Awakens</i>, therefore these things are not popular or selling well.&quot; It's one of the dumbest things in all of fandom and almost always done disingenuously. V5 is doing fine, better than fine, and penetrating multiple markets. It's also only beginning its career.<br /> <br /> If people want to discuss the success, make a new thread but there will be no spreading of this idea.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-12-2020, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T06:52:34-07:00","id":1417805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please don't insinuate that I and others who disagree with V5's stances are just... Toreador.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't. I gave the Toreador as an optional toy to play with while you wait for something different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, grand sweeping changes like the second largest sect buggering off into the middle east, leaving their cities open to whatever... The Camarilla giving up it's monopoly and a big part of it's identity, the brujah leaving the Camarilla for a contrivance.... not to mention the huge sweeping mechanical changes.<br /> <br /> &quot;fans react poorly to grand sweeping changes&quot; so we did just that...<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be mistaken: I don't run my V5 games incorporating every change made to this edition, and like all other fans, I'm waiting to see how it resolves in print. But the difference is, I don't equate my waiting with suffering or express that change is needed <b>right now</b>. Mechanical changes are, however (and in my opinion), good for a new edition, and the Brujah leaving the Camarilla has been a long time coming. As for the Camarilla becoming a more clandestine, elite organisation, I'm all for it. <br /> <br /> As I said, vagueness is a deliberate choice. We chose to be vague about some things, clear about others. If we went wholly one way, we'd still be looking at a group of unhappy older fans. Star Wars is the most demonstrable license where they did this very thing. Fans are fans, some are entitled, some want things to remain the way they've always loved them, others adapt, others embrace changes. You can slot yourself wherever you want, and I know there are some things I'd have preferred remain as they were in V20 and prior, but that just means when I run games I do just that. It's easy when you do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(V5 totally took a political stance and told some players they were playing it wrong. I am not of that political persuasion, but it came off as an unpleasant, It really does tell players they're playing a game wrong)</span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The V5 stance on the political spectrum is not new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the surface that's a fine rationale, but it breaks apart in reality. When everyone's mostly on the same page after reading the same book, with perhaps some different interpretations, that's great. When it becomes the norm for fans to need to justify their changes and establish what they want out of playing a certain clan when the fluff and rules no longer support the vision they had built up. Players and storytellers need to be on the same page and treated fairly. If the Storyteller wants to make changes, say they want to use something from first edition instead of V5, it is a little bit inconvenient for players who actually liked the v5 writeup more and had invested themselves into their character through that (especially if the shuffle comes late) whilst, if I wanted to play a Classic Tremere, steeped in a Hermetic paradigm, who creates all sorts of miracles with his will rather than play NuTremere who's really just a blood bender with some rituals, I'd need to demand concessions from my storyteller, and then I'd be <i>that Guy. </i><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not inconvenient if the players and ST discuss what they want ahead of the game. It's actually very easy. It's why there's a Kiasyd in my V5 game, a cleric of a god dead in the present Forgotten Realms in my Pathfinder game, a lady knight in my Pendragon game, and a character with hedge magic in my Call of Cthulhu game. Improvisation and adapting to one's gaming group is the mark of a decent Storyteller, just as the players investing in a new world can be an exciting experience for them, if they want to do it. I'd advise against <b>demanding</b> concessions from your Storyteller, because yes, you would indeed be <i>that guy</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope.Let me stop you there: I saw the table. I have not stated anything concerning the power of elders without considering the table. It is not a good table.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of whether or not you like the table, you're not addressing the various factors I presented that make elders more powerful than fledglings. They are, and as Scott Steiner says: the numbers don't lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the first time in five editions, not counting for the dark ages, where thin blood is considered 'a step beyond regular vampires'. If we were to consider the subject of alchemy properly, you'd quickly realise they're the result of an incomplete alchemical process: Mortals are lead, Caine is Gold. Mortals are at 0, Caine is a step below God. actual alchemy is deeper than the DnD stuff, and it's a shame thin bloods get this flimsy power to give them a nice happy niche and discourage them from actually joining the Jyhad proper.<br /> as thin bloods do not have access to normal disciplines for some reason in V5, it might as well be obligatory, because there is no alternative to them acquiring magic power.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it is a new move because very few people played thin-bloods in previous editions (which were introduced in third edition and changed in V20, so every edition has been different). As for whether thin-bloods can access normal Disciplines, they can, and there's a Merit for it. I recommend re-reading that section of the book again, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -If Dominate crushes your mystery plot you'd better come up with better plots. Combine it with obfuscate, or use that -only one Dominate at a time- rule that seems to have been forgotten.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, or you can use the new version of Dominate. Entirely up to you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Potence, as just strength, was elegant in it's intuitive simplicity. It would help you jump, climb, swim, grapple, pounce, throw... V5 potence is absurd. &quot;Do I learn to jump or do I learn to cause lethal damage with my fists? I must keep in mind that being able to jump real high does nothing for kicks or...&quot; like, what?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Customisation is good. It makes characters stand apart from each other. I you want Potence to cover every physical action, I'd suggest you're looking for an overpowered Discipline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - not making easy sense preserves the mystery and allows for different branches of occultism to arise; Don't fucking solve our answers for us. How can an abyss mystic be taken seriously when their musings of 'a realm outside of creation' are just answered by 'yo it's this thing at the bottom of the underworld, get off your high horse!' How many characters are you killing by giving easy answers to what should be difficult questions? Plus, and you'll have to bare with me on this one: The Abyss being wraith's Oblivion is just a shit solution. Also it begs the question as to how Giovanni and Lasombra weren't once identical bloodlines because before the feast they had the exact same disciplines... oh yeah, the weakness. You've all really fucked up the occultism factor of this kinda thing, for Lasombra and all the necromancers too.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You're starting to swear at this point and it's not conducive to a reasonable discussion. Maybe take a break from the internet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, I was extremely happy to play Caitiffs and thinbloods before they got their snowflake power that makes them absurdly useful. I fill my dark ages games with an abundanced of nuanced Lasombra, some of my favourites are positively timid. The issue is, in V5, they are absolutely shoe-horned in as fools and whipping boys. Thats their 'new role'. Where before I could play them in any number of ways, now they're a C-list clan.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny you say that, because Talley, Sierra, and Malenkov in Chicago by Night are none of them &quot;fools and whipping boys&quot;. I suggest examining the way you play them if you can't work out how to play an interesting Lasombra in V5. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It dropped off the RPG best sellers list, did it not? The Prior edition does seem to be holding more steady. (though I'll admit, this is through online sales and V5 has the huge advantage of being in stores) &quot;going back to a prior edition&quot; is not a great suggestion, marketing wise.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not in marketing, but buying books for previous editions, published by the same company, still generates income. V5 is selling well enough for Paradox, from across multiple venues and in multiple languages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the latter- Ok, that's good. Point conceeded.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I could help!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To Thaumaturgy: Your assertion is derived from an incomplete understanding of what thaumaturgy is. Thaumaturgy is not 'blood magic' it's miracle working. Vitae is a sacrifice because vampires store their magic juice there. Saying it's gotta be 'blood themed magic' is like saying nuclear power should only be used to power nuclear technologies: behold my uranium lightbulb.<br /> Nah seriously, Did you think when people wrote the first edition the people who made Tremere a bunch of Western-tradition Hermetic mages were somehow misguided in adding multiple paths, paths like the lure of flames, and that they didn't know what they were talking about and should've kept everything blood-themed with maybe some curses mixed in? That sounds positively juvenile.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're being unpleasant and &quot;name-calling&quot; at this point, so once I've made this comment, I won't be responding to you further. Try engaging with people in a courteous way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"> Also have you read Mage: The Ascension by any chance? </span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the game's under my bracket as the World of Darkness developer and I've ran it and written for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417799#post1417799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much of the people who seem to be enjoying this edition's Lasombra seem to be the people who did not enjoy the Lasombra in the last one. I've seen nothing but anguish concerning Oblivion. Many are still upset the Sabbat are gone. The point of praise seems to be the new weakness: The old weakness seemed like 'not a problem' till you really thought about it, and thus this praise is not from people who 'really thought about it' (and thus played the clan)<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd advise against insulting a proportion of the fanbase by saying they didn't really think about the Lasombra weakness, and thereby weren't playing the clan properly. That's a bit gatekeepery, and I'd prefer people just play however they like. As for anguish regarding Oblivion, I must disagree as I'm happy to say I've seen and heard from a lot of people who like Oblivion now, when they disliked Obtenebration before. Different strokes for different folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T06:56:17-07:00","id":1417806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't be mistaken: I don't run my V5 games incorporating every change made to this edition, and like all other fans, I'm waiting to see how it resolves in print.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is very important to remember for every gamer. Everyone's table is different even if you follow all of the rules and setting changes, everyone has a different interpretation of the nature of these things.<br /> <br /> I admit, I barely paid any attention to the changes to Dominate regarding the ability to force people to tell the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T06:58:28-07:00","id":1417807,"title":"","content":"Nothing wrong with a nice happy niche...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T07:05:45-07:00","id":1417808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417807#post1417807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing wrong with a nice happy niche...</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest benefit of these forums is really a discussion and sharing of how you interpret a character, setting, Clan, Discipline, or use some rules while discarding others.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, The Storyteller is always RightTM.<br /> <br /> And what is fun should always be the most important rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T07:13:29-07:00","id":1417809,"title":"","content":"Oh, one last thing:<br /> <br /> <br /> Clan Lasombra didn't join the Camarilla. Several vampires of Clan Lasombra did.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's an important distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T07:24:46-07:00","id":1417812,"title":"","content":"On a completely unrelated note:<br /> <br /> I really wish we'd find out Lucita's fate. Did Talley REALLY send her to the Final Death? I never liked they turned her into just another Sabbat stooge (and a child killer to boot) but I'm still invested in her storyline.<br /> <br /> It'd be interesting to see how she would react to the fact that no sooner does she join the Sabbat after 800 years but:<br /> <br /> 1. Gehenna happens and its very likely the Sabbat ran right into the fangs of the Antediluvians.<br /> 2. All of the Lasombra find out the Antediluvian is alive.<br /> 3. The Amis Noctis' response is to join the Camarilla because, &quot;Well, we failed to kill him. Now we should join the side that are the Antediluvian's pawns.&quot;<br /> 4. The Sabbat effectively collapses into either remnants (The Seven Fires), is defeated by the Second Inquisition/Camarilla, or joins the rest of the Gehenna Crusade.<br /> <br /> I feel like this would make an awesome novel.<br /> <br /> Called, &quot;This was a terrible idea.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T08:25:02-07:00","id":1417820,"title":"","content":"I hope they don't...I would eventually like to be able to play my favorite sect again :-(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T08:27:30-07:00","id":1417821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417812#post1417812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish we'd find out Lucita's fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt she is actually dead, but we will probably get an answer in either the <i>Players Guide </i>or the eventual <i>Sabbat </i>book.Or possibly one of the books following <i>Cults of Blood</i> gods (i.e. <i>Forbidden Religions </i>or <i>Children of Blood</i>).<br /> <br /> Edit: At a guess she will emerge as a leader of a Sabbat survivor cell, and have a Magneto type of roll. Kind of a hard ass, not willing to compromise their survival or freedom, but not unhinged or wanting to destroy the world either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-12-2020, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T08:46:13-07:00","id":1417824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417820#post1417820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they don't...I would eventually like to be able to play my favorite sect again :-(</div> </div> </div> </div>My hope is there's multiple Sabbats that get created from this.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a Book of Sabbats with variations that emphasize different types. The cult Sabbat, the Black Hand, the Satanic demon worshiping ones, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T08:58:16-07:00","id":1417827,"title":"","content":"Ya Id rather they not take a VII and Belial's Brood approach to muh favorite sect lol. Anymore then I am sure you would want them to do that to the Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:08:03-07:00","id":1417830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417827#post1417827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya Id rather they not take a VII and Belial's Brood approach to muh favorite sect lol. Anymore then I am sure you would want them to do that to the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's what I love about V5's Anarchs. They ditched the &quot;Every Anarch is an LA gang member&quot; to embrace the diversity of Antifa, Soviet Communists, Fascist Warlords, Neo-Confederates, Hippies, Cult Leaders, and more.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not really ANARCHY if it's all just one group.<br /> <br /> But I admit part of this is because I'd like to have a bigger diversity of the Sabbat. I love the Loyalists but no way in hell do they get along with the Black Hand. I also feel like there should be a city for my Path of Harmony City Gangrel!<br /> <br /> *weeps at Revised saying she was killed for being sweet*<br /> <br /> The Sabbat being divided into multiple groups, each claiming to be the &quot;real&quot; Sabbat would be cool and doesn't have to last forever. Eventually, one true leader would emerge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:13:13-07:00","id":1417832,"title":"","content":"See I find a LOT of diversity in Revised Era Sabbat. I think Mexico City by Night did a great job fleshing out the fact that the Sabbat is really a sect of factions and each with a very different political agenda and what the sabbat means to each of them. I have actually been working on an STV book for some time that goes in depth into the Sabbat Factions and the diversity of the sect. Just waiting for my artist to finish :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:13:37-07:00","id":1417833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417830#post1417830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, that's what I love about V5's Anarchs. They ditched the &amp;quot;Every Anarch is an LA gang member&amp;quot; to embrace the diversity of Antifa, Soviet Communists, Fascist Warlords, Neo-Confederates, Hippies, Cult Leaders, and more.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not really ANARCHY if it's all just one group.<br /> <br /> But I admit part of this is because I'd like to have a bigger diversity of the Sabbat. I love the Loyalists but no way in hell do they get along with the Black Hand. I also feel like there should be a city for my Path of Harmony City Gangrel!<br /> <br /> *weeps at Revised saying she was killed for being sweet*<br /> <br /> The Sabbat being divided into multiple groups, each claiming to be the &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; Sabbat would be cool and doesn't have to last forever. Eventually, one true leader would emerge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Path of Harmony City Gangrel sounds really sweet \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> I do think the Sabbat surviving in fragmented form sounds like a great idea. So does bringing back previously rejected Paths like Harmony and Lilith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:35:03-07:00","id":1417837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417832#post1417832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I find a LOT of diversity in Revised Era Sabbat. I think Mexico City by Night did a great job fleshing out the fact that the Sabbat is really a sect of factions and each with a very different political agenda and what the sabbat means to each of them. I have actually been working on an STV book for some time that goes in depth into the Sabbat Factions and the diversity of the sect. Just waiting for my artist to finish :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll definitely buy a copy. I admit, I am going to say that the Sabbat is not gone in my home games and I've flat out ignores some of V5's changes for them.<br /> <br /> <b>How CT Phipps Runs the Sabbat in V5</b><br /> <br /> * The Sabbat is REDUCED but not destroyed or all off in the Gehenna Crusade.<br /> <br /> * The loss of Mexico City and Montreal as well as the fact they're the obvious targets for the Second Inquisition [with the help of the Camarilla] hit them hard. So did defections to the Anarchs, Church of Caine, and other Blood Cults.<br /> <br /> * Polonia won the Regency of the Sabbat and led the majority of the Sabbat's military forces through the Middle East but they're not the totality of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> * Already a bunch of Low Generation Sabbat warped by the souls of the ancient Kindred they've fed upon are returning and forming their own cults as well as branches of the organization. These are a bunch of mysterious and unpleasant Kindred who are more or less rebuilding the &quot;True Hand&quot; (without the joke elements) within the Sabbat as Antediluvian worshiping Fifth Columnists.<br /> <br /> * Miami, Juarez/El Paso, Detroit, Kansas City, San Salvador, and a handful of other cities are &quot;Fortress Cities&quot; where the Sabbat rule and are independently maintained by Archbishops. Basically, look up &quot;Most Violent Cities in the World&quot; for which cities the Sabbat still control. The exceptions are Saint Paul and Baltimore.<br /> <br /> * The fortress cities give Polonia only the barest of acknowledgements and quite a few consider other parties to be Regents or themselves in the role. Polonia doesn't have the reach to dissuade these &quot;traitor&quot; Sabbat.<br /> <br /> * The Tremere antitribu are back, ruled by &quot;Goratrix.&quot; Given he's an Antediluvian, this is incredibly hilarious. He's also why the Sabbat around him are utterly safe from Camarilla oppression. Oddly, he's allied with the Salubri Antitribu who have put aside their ancient feud.<br /> <br /> * The Tzimisce have made peace with the Old Clan and are acting as an independent clan for the most part. Members maintain Sabbat menbership and defend their packs but have largely decided the Sabbat is a failed experiment. Half of the Tzimisce remain commited and are usually the rulers of the most stable Fortress Cities.<br /> <br /> * Lucita is missing and is considered &quot;The Real Regent&quot; by many who hate Polonia.<br /> <br /> * The Ministry includes many Serpents of Light who helped them defect. This is looked at with suspicion by other Sabbat.<br /> <br /> * A lot of Sabbat have gone &quot;undercover&quot; in Camarilla or Anarch cities with the defecting Lasombra. They believe the Lasombra are playing the long game and that they'll rejoin the Sabbat or revolt when the Sabbat gets their shit straight. Whether this is true or not doesn't matter as they're allies with the new defectors. Quite a few find that the local Blood Cults and tolerated viciousness (as long as its hidden) isn't THAT different.<br /> <br /> * Devil worship is now tolerated in many domains where the Inquisition is weak. This pisses them off to no end. However, the Sabbat have plenty of people who don't see anything wrong with the aid of demons. The Path of the Devil has replaced the Path of Evil Revelations and is the fastest growing religion among Sabbat.<br /> <br /> * The Grimaldi have defected to the Giovanni and Pentex, working to destroy their former masters.<br /> <br /> * For all the shit the Sabbat have taken, the Gehenna Crusade has killed more Elders of the Camarilla that arrived via the Beckoning than the previous 600 years combined. They have also destroyed multiple 4th generation vampires and seriously impacted the post-Crusade Jyhad--if there is one.<br /> <br /> * Thin Bloods are officially considered vermin and to be &quot;cured&quot; by offering them diablerie. Some Sabbat believe their powers warrants membership, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-12-2020, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:40:13-07:00","id":1417839,"title":"","content":"I like most of what you have done with them considering the current v5 canon. A lot of that makes sense. I do think the Sabbat need a &quot;Capital&quot; as it was Mexico City. Would be slightly terrifying if it was...Oh I dunno Jerusalem now lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:45:21-07:00","id":1417842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417839#post1417839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like most of what you have done with them considering the current v5 canon. A lot of that makes sense. I do think the Sabbat need a &quot;Capital&quot; as it was Mexico City. Would be slightly terrifying if it was...Oh I dunno Jerusalem now lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Libya seems like a good place to put the Sabbat capital because it's far away from the Middle East that presumably it's not TOTALLY under Antediluvian control. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You could also be hilarious with the Sabbat being all based in Dubai but on their best behavior.<br /> <br /> Polonia having a big old penthouse and ordering around people via cellphone.<br /> <br /> I have a lot of the Sabbat's battles also taking place in Saudi Arabia's &quot;Empty Quarter&quot; just because there's nothing there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-12-2020, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:52:10-07:00","id":1417843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417805#post1417805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't be mistaken: I don't run my V5 games incorporating every change made to this edition, and like all other fans, I'm waiting to see how it resolves in print. But the difference is, I don't equate my waiting with suffering or express that change is needed <b>right now</b>. Mechanical changes are, however (and in my opinion), good for a new edition, and the Brujah leaving the Camarilla has been a long time coming. As for the Camarilla becoming a more clandestine, elite organisation, I'm all for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla changing it's face is something that I think might become a very good thing. It might also... not really go where I'm hoping it will and just be a foil for the much cooler anarchs. A Monopoly is a powerful thing, and they gave it up; there best be a clever reason for that.<br /> <br /> As for Brujah; Disagree strongly. They're always fighting themselves, so they'd never let someone with a weird idea spoil it for the rest of them. There's no way they could possibly agree to losing their seat at the table. Many, many Brujah (and it is a big, big clan) would surely want to remain within the Camarilla, and they surely wouldn't the actions of one of their number screw the whole clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The V5 stance on the political spectrum is not new. </div> </div> </div>Stance and approach are two different things. This is... off topic, but I thought one of the golden rules of writing was to 'show, not tell'? I want a subversive masterpiece, not a tirade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not inconvenient if the players and ST discuss what they want ahead of the game. It's actually very easy. It's why there's a Kiasyd in my V5 game, a cleric of a god dead in the present Forgotten Realms in my Pathfinder game, a lady knight in my Pendragon game, and a character with hedge magic in my Call of Cthulhu game. Improvisation and adapting to one's gaming group is the mark of a decent Storyteller, just as the players investing in a new world can be an exciting experience for them, if they want to do it. I'd advise against <b>demanding</b> concessions from your Storyteller, because yes, you would indeed be <i>that guy</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regardless of whether or not you like the table, you're not addressing the various factors I presented that make elders more powerful than fledglings. They are, and as Scott Steiner says: the numbers don't lie. </div> </div> </div>The numbers suggest a methuselah would be in a bit of trouble against four neonates, and quite screwed against more. Of course, a competent Methuselah would never suffer such odds, but V5 has flattened the power curve quite a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yep, it is a new move because very few people played thin-bloods in previous editions (which were introduced in third edition and changed in V20, so every edition has been different). As for whether thin-bloods can access normal Disciplines, they can, and there's a Merit for it. I recommend re-reading that section of the book again, too. </div> </div> </div>If you wanted more people to play thinbloods, a thematic change was all that's neccessary. People weren't discoraged by thinbloods because they were weak, they were discouraged because you weren't really supposed to play them or hang with them for social or political reasons. Now that Anarchs seem to be the default faction or near enough, that should be enough to play them.<br /> Giving them an absurd drug cooking power that'll make a Tremere want to self immolate is not the answer to a 'problem' that infact a feature.<br /> <br /> Vampire was about ambition. Between the new generation rules and thin bloods getting unique toys, it seems the message is 'be happy about knowing your place'. <i>Some people are just born stronger than you, and you should accept that, if you be like them you'll be a sinner and you'll be sick with your sin. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Customisation is good. It makes characters stand apart from each other. I you want Potence to cover every physical action, I'd suggest you're looking for an overpowered Discipline. </div> </div> </div>Potence was not considered overpowered in any edition before it. You should also look into the concept of overchoice: simple is good. New players should just chose the discipline that sounds good, not have to map a path to power or else screw themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's funny you say that, because Talley, Sierra, and Malenkov in Chicago by Night are none of them &quot;fools and whipping boys&quot;. I suggest examining the way you play them if you can't work out how to play an interesting Lasombra in V5. </div> </div> </div>Storyteller characters don't suffer from the rigors a player character has to go through. I've seen a couple of characters that surely<i> would not fly</i> if a player made them.<br /> (reading the specifics on such characters would require me to buy the book)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd advise against insulting a proportion of the fanbase by saying they didn't really think about the Lasombra weakness, and thereby weren't playing the clan properly. That's a bit gatekeepery, and I'd prefer people just play however they like. As for anguish regarding Oblivion, I must disagree as I'm happy to say I've seen and heard from a lot of people who like Oblivion now, when they disliked Obtenebration before. Different strokes for different folks. </div> </div> </div>Obtenebration was too strong. No argument there. The clan also attracted and encouraged 'that guy' while now it doesn't do such.<br /> But oblivion...<br /> I suppose Lasombra can enjoy necromancy now. That stuff might be totally great if you are new or otherwise didn't care for the Lasombra identity. But shadow play? nah. It's less useful than that one path Tremere made to combat Lasombra, which was budget darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tremere </div> </div> </div>Look, I like playing a genuine OG wizard in my vampire games. The philosophy, the organization, the power you could in-character gloat about but not-really because it's expensive and not all that powerful if you don't take a few broken paths? Great stuff.<br /> <br /> V5, in this among other things, has cut off my options. Sure I can join House Carna now (I can even pretend I don't know it's a sham and even go along with the idea that you don't need discipline, training and a viable paradigm) but I can't fly or throw fire or become one with the machine or speak with the spirits or do some wicked-sick gardening or invest far too many experience points into creating a dope-ass magic sword (I might still be able to make the sword, but not to the extent of prior)<br /> <br /> My options as a Tremere are inexplicably gone because a few people have decided the so-far normal idea of a vampire sorcerer no longer fits the narrow vision of what they think vampire sorcerers should be doing. Apparently I can no longer be an Abyss mystic because it's gone from merely -sketchy- to -infernal- (and also the Abyss really lost it's interest). Oh and I'd struggle to ask to be a proper wizard again because it's maybe-balanced against everything else, XP is weird now, and... Quietus is now Thaumaturgy because fuck their culture and the culture of sorcerers everywhere.<br /> For all the options V5 has added it's sure slammed down a lot of new restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:53:27-07:00","id":1417844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417830#post1417830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sabbat being divided into multiple groups, each claiming to be the &quot;real&quot; Sabbat would be cool and doesn't have to last forever. Eventually, one true leader would emerge.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the 4th Sabbat Civil War would end up like the 2nd one, with one strong leader emerging to lead them, just like Galbraith did?<br /> <br /> As a fan of &quot;History Doesn't Repeat Itself, but It Often Rhymes&quot; thing, I'd like to see that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:54:17-07:00","id":1417845,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> <br /> You can do all of that stuff.<br /> <br /> Lure of the Flames isn't gone, it's just a ritual now. It's one shot a night like D&amp;D but it's the same powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: The Vinculum</b><br /> <br /> I think it'd be interesting if the Amis Noctis arranged for large numbers of the Lasombra to &quot;visit&quot; them at the Castle of Shadows in Spain as part of their defection to the Camarilla. Obviously, the ones in the Gehenna Crusade won't come (or maybe they would) but the ones left behind would just have to make arrangements. There, the Amis Noctis can use a combination of Abyssal Mysticism or Blood Sorcery to up the Vinculum enough to break their loyalties to their Packs or the Sabbat in general.<br /> <br /> Is this violating the spirit of the Sabbat? OF COURSE.<br /> <br /> But who cares?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T10:05:46-07:00","id":1417847,"title":"","content":"I like the idea in Chicago by Night that the Lasombra defected to the Camarilla as a possible trojan horse for the Sabbat....but i am also a Sabbat Fanboy. It does seem that with Coteries of New York (for example) they are walking back that it was &quot;Half of Clan Lasombra&quot; that defected and more like &quot;A handful&quot; with them talking about how its kind of a Chicago thing where the body of the Camarilla Lasombra exists (there's obviously at least 2 in New York). But that seems...less then &quot;Half of the Clan&quot;. Or perhaps that's just how I read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T10:56:27-07:00","id":1417850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417847#post1417847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea in Chicago by Night that the Lasombra defected to the Camarilla as a possible trojan horse for the Sabbat....but i am also a Sabbat Fanboy. It does seem that with Coteries of New York (for example) they are walking back that it was &quot;Half of Clan Lasombra&quot; that defected and more like &quot;A handful&quot; with them talking about how its kind of a Chicago thing where the body of the Camarilla Lasombra exists (there's obviously at least 2 in New York). But that seems...less then &quot;Half of the Clan&quot;. Or perhaps that's just how I read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's less than half the Clan, it's silly, because they'd be sacrificing themselves in the Gehenna Crusade and lose one of their awesome moments of treachery.<br /> <br /> They would also not be offering much to the Camarilla or warrant a Justicar or Inner Council.<br /> <br /> Mind you, there's only about 2000 of every Clan in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <