r":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T13:33:38-07:00","id":1417897,"title":"","content":"I tried watching LA by Night when it came out. I dunno, wasn't really my thing. I am more of a Critical Role kind of guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T15:54:44-07:00","id":1417940,"title":"","content":"I remember Vitel from BJD. He was the most powerful of the antitribu (except for maybe Montano?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T15:59:04-07:00","id":1417941,"title":"","content":"Marcus Vitel was (might still be) a hilarious 90s Super Villain of a vampire. &quot;Huzzah! I now possess the Nuclear Launch Codes of the United States and Shall take over the World!&quot; (That's a real thing for that character)....and I love him. He is the Cobra Commander of Vampire the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T16:13:09-07:00","id":1417943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417941#post1417941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marcus Vitel was (might still be) a hilarious 90s Super Villain of a vampire. &quot;Huzzah! I now possess the Nuclear Launch Codes of the United States and Shall take over the World!&quot; (That's a real thing for that character)....and I love him. He is the Cobra Commander of Vampire the Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games, Vitel is the guy behind the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> Just straight up, he's the guy who protects all the Second Inquisition higher ups and told them all about vampires in order to make sure it was impossible for the Camarilla to shut down. The War on Terror impressed him so much that he abandoned the whole nuclear war plan (it only half-worked on the Ravnos antediluvian) and now thinks if he kills half or 2/3rds of the vampire race that he can just step in as God Emperor.<br /> <br /> He's also the guy who bombed Alamut (which was bombed by the US military in my games).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417940#post1417940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Vitel from BJD. He was the most powerful of the antitribu (except for maybe Montano?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Was he Antitribu? He was part of the Camarilla but feeding the Sabbat information. Given he was 2000 years old, I imagined he found both sects...silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T16:43:09-07:00","id":1417949,"title":"","content":"Hahahaha! VtM: Rise of Vitel needs to be a book now. Ala GI JOE: Rise of Cobra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T18:10:31-07:00","id":1417963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417856#post1417856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually always assumed their number was in the low hundreds, like most bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never assigned them any numbers, but I had a general idea in my head that the Lasombra AT were &quot;confined&quot; to a handful of cities or regions within the general Camarilla domain. That was mainly several cities in Spain/Portugal, Italy, the Southern Cone and Brazil in South America, the Maghreb, and a few other random cities that would be considered &quot;non-traditional&quot; for Lasombra. In those cities, they were essentially the eighth clan of the Camarilla locally. But they were absent elsewhere for a variety of reasons. One was that Lasombra AT that left the nest to be by themselves without other Lasombra AT around them were easily prone to being slain by roving Sabbat (or have other mysterious deaths/disappearances). Another was that few Camarilla Princes outside those domains wanted a Lasombra AT in their domain, and they were heavily discouraged from visiting or staying. That was either out of a desire for less competition from another clan; old grudges against the clan; or not wanting to attract Sabbat attacks. The British Isles in particular were known to be free of them.<br /> <br /> So there easily could have been one or two hundred. (In contrast, I think most bloodlines have far fewer numbers than you. I imagined most bloodlines to be in the dozens, not hundreds.)<br /> <br /> I held that Sabbat statements about having destroyed almost all the Lasombra AT were mainly propaganda and hyperbole combined with ignorance as to the true state of many Camarilla domains.<br /> <br /> Like all things, depending on one's assumptions and tastes, you can have a wide variety of answers and fit within canon lore.<br /> <br /> One reason I wanted a noticeable, albeit still rare, presence in the Camarilla is that I thought much of the clan's description in the clanbooks made sense for a Camarilla clan, but a lot less for the Sabbat. A major problem I had with the Sabbat was the clanbooks acting like the two Sabbat clans were similar to the Camarilla clans instead of being heavily influenced by the Anarch Revolt and the institutions and culture of the Sabbat. I briefly discussed that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates/page9\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates/page10\">here</a>. So in my own chronicles I altered the Sabbat versions of the clan to better reflect that. As a result, some of the interesting aspects of the Lasombra were excised from the Sabbat, so I made them a prominent part of the culture of the anti-tribu in the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T19:46:42-07:00","id":1417980,"title":"","content":"My opinion is contrary to most in that I'm not a huge fan of Clan Lasombra in general. Too much of the &quot;Real, ultimate vampires&quot; schlock turns me off. Whatever they are trying to pull off, Ventrue and Giovanni do it better.<br /> <br /> The writing behind the exodus makes sense, but in my headcannon it would only be a small crescent of the Clan that makes the move, the Social Darwinian &quot;pinnacle of excellence,&quot; &quot;like Ventrue, but better,&quot; &quot;I can spell Machiavellian&quot; extremely vocal minority who don't have the chops to stick it out against the Big Bads like the rest of the clan (Abyss Mystics, etc). These types are a good fit to fill the niches of &quot;annoying thorn in Ventrue sides&quot; and &quot;can punch real hard&quot; left by the departing Brujah, always angling for position but never quite coming out ahead. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T01:51:54-07:00","id":1417999,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1417884]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I admit, I've always had a view that the Sabbat was a lot smarter than people gave it credit for. The shovelheads and Mass Embraced psychopaths losing themselves to the Beast were a danger, yes, but before things started to go to hell with the East Coast Crusade, the majority of Sabbat were a lot more subtle than they were reputed to be. How does a Sabbat member infiltrate the Camarilla? </div> </div> </div> I agree. To me the Sabbat is composed of clever manipulators who usually don't really hold the sects ideals to heart, or go along with them for fun, and cannon fodder (Much like the Anarchs) This thus makes me question the Sabbats commitment to a middle-eastern crusade. Almost certainly the Sect feels it has too many surviving neonates causing trouble and wants to kill em off. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Antitribu puts on a nice jacket, walks in to Elysium, introduces himself to the Prince and agrees to bide by the Traditions. He then locates the Lasombra Antitribu and blows up his or her car before slipping out. </div> </div> </div>This is how you get yourself killed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dunno, isn't Thaumaturgy MORE powerful at the 1-5 level now? You can learn Path of Flames, Neptune's Fury, or the Spirit Thaumaturgy Paths just by learning rituals now -- and they don't cost EXP. </div> </div> </div>I thought they do cost XP now? <br /> <br /> And yeah, again, your at-will machinegun has been replaced with a special matchlock you need to spend 5/10/15 minutes to prepare before firing. Also, it's not just the power levels, it's the experience and the fluff behind it. I can feel powerful and show off if I can do nonsense like use lure-of-flames 1 to fulfil the function of a cigarete lighter, or if I can grab my umbrella by just reaching for it, or if an unexpected obstacle appears in my way i can just fly over it or force-lift it(or imolate/destroy it) Having to go through lengthly rituals to do simple things like this is just lame. <br /> <br /> The Old Thaumaturgy was not broke. It did not need fixing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought it was a bit weird myself but I remember that conversation differently than you do. Talley talked to Theo Bell in that bar and he asked, &quot;Do you really believe the bullshit about the sects being different?&quot; Theo Bell saying he did surprised Talley because the implications I got was Talley thought the Sabbat was a JOB, not a vocation. </div> </div> </div>I can agree with the sentiment. The overwhelming majority of sectarian ideals are just there to keep the neonates doing what you want them to do. Honestly the Anarchs are probably the worst for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T05:22:02-07:00","id":1418024,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=MyWifeIsScary;n1417999]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417884#post1417884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. To me the Sabbat is composed of clever manipulators who usually don't really hold the sects ideals to heart, or go along with them for fun, and cannon fodder (Much like the Anarchs) This thus makes me question the Sabbats commitment to a middle-eastern crusade. Almost certainly the Sect feels it has too many surviving neonates causing trouble and wants to kill em off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, I fully see that happening ala THE GREAT LEAP OUTWARD. However, the difference is when the Lasombra Elder pulls this and doesn't go themselves, the Neonates turn on the cowar,d kill him, kill his court, and WIN. The numbers and veteran status of the &quot;insane bloodthirsty psychopath&quot; Sabbat far exceed those of the clever manipulative Sabbat. The mob is something they lost control of at some point and they must either join their insane quest or defect.<br /> <br /> I personally blame the East Coast Crusade. The Sabbat in North America expanded in size a dozen times over and began a massive war with the American Camarilla that resulted in the creation of thousands of shovelheads for all the cities they created and then all of these became battle hardened survivors. So when the Lasombra planned to pull their usual tricks, they found a bunch of paranoid Beast-ridden psychos who had glutted themselves on the diablerie of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I had the funny idea that Polonia didn't intend to FIND anything in the Middle East. He just was the most unlucky Regent in a history of unlucky Regents.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> I actually added an idea of how this went down here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1418026#post1418026\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...26#post1418026</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is how you get yourself killed. </div> </div> </div>No, because Sabbat agents are smarter than Camarilla ones. There's entire books about Sabbat infiltrators and they will fool Camarilla Primogens and Princes 9/10. The &quot;open door policy&quot; of the Camarilla almost always ends in the Sabbat's favor.<br /> <br /> Sabbat infiltrators almost ALWAYS accomplish their mission.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought they do cost XP now? </div> </div> </div>Weird typo on my part as it was meant to be &quot;much EXP&quot; but the sentence still made sense (and was wrong). My bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yeah, again, your at-will machinegun has been replaced with a special matchlock you need to spend 5/10/15 minutes to prepare before firing. </div> </div> </div>Actually, you can store it. So you do the 5-10 minute ritual and then go, &quot;Ignis&quot; so it fires.<br /> <br /> It's still weaker than Lure of the Flames but it's not THAT much weaker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can agree with the sentiment. The overwhelming majority of sectarian ideals are just there to keep the neonates doing what you want them to do. Honestly the Anarchs are probably the worst for this. </div> </div> </div>Agreed, which is why Talley went along with the orders he got. He was the most &quot;loyal&quot; Sabbat for 600 years because he just obeyed orders without any personal ambition or care about the ideology about them. To be a traitor in the Sabbat, you normally have to care about something enough to believe you have to fight for it. But as we see with the Sabbat and other leadership, if you keep trying to manipulate the mob, it will turn on you.<br /> <br /> It's why the Antitribu turned on the Lasombra, it's why the Brujah and Gangrel turned on the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-13-2020, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T00:43:42-07:00","id":1418153,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1418024]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417999#post1417999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, I fully see that happening ala THE GREAT LEAP OUTWARD. However, the difference is when the Lasombra Elder pulls this and doesn't go themselves, the Neonates turn on the cowar,d kill him, kill his court, and WIN. The numbers and veteran status of the &quot;insane bloodthirsty psychopath&quot; Sabbat far exceed those of the clever manipulative Sabbat. The mob is something they lost control of at some point and they must either join their insane quest or defect.<br /> <br /> I personally blame the East Coast Crusade. The Sabbat in North America expanded in size a dozen times over and began a massive war with the American Camarilla that resulted in the creation of thousands of shovelheads for all the cities they created and then all of these became battle hardened survivors. So when the Lasombra planned to pull their usual tricks, they found a bunch of paranoid Beast-ridden psychos who had glutted themselves on the diablerie of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Battle hardened psychos that have had far less opportunity and capability to accumulate resources, retainers, and other defences. Besides, these elders are unlikely to be strangers to battle, and they may take advantage of veteran overconfidence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, I had the funny idea that Polonia didn't intend to FIND anything in the Middle East. He just was the most unlucky Regent in a history of unlucky Regents. </div> </div> </div>It's all a big scam so the elders can kill of their neonates in shipping crates and join the nuCamarilla. Calling it (well, I called it before but...)<br /> Anything else is silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, because Sabbat agents are smarter than Camarilla ones. There's entire books about Sabbat infiltrators and they will fool Camarilla Primogens and Princes 9/10. The &quot;open door policy&quot; of the Camarilla almost always ends in the Sabbat's favor.<br /> <br /> Sabbat infiltrators almost ALWAYS accomplish their mission. </div> </div> </div>So, the book I've read on the topic suggested that although the sabbat understoon the basics of how Camarilla society works, much of the intricacies and perculiarities of courts elude them and cause them to stick out. In the example given, I think you would get caught trying to 'find the Lasombra'; an established Lasombra would probably lobby elysium to take place with no or few mirrors, or they'd avoid the non-essential Elysiums in places with many (and if you're using the V5 weakness, it's a little harder to find them stick out) and going around trying to look into something reflective or using a bug is undoubtedly something that will be noticed by the absurdly keen eyes of the auspex users there. If the prince is particularly paranoid and the entree is suspicious (Say, they have no relfection) there are tests they can be subjected to. The question on if the intruder survives the night is really up to the court: They may lose face if the Lasombra Antitribu dies to a Sabbat Assassin. It might be in their personal interests to turn a blind eye to a potential killing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, you can store it. So you do the 5-10 minute ritual and then go, &quot;Ignis&quot; so it fires.<br /> <br /> It's still weaker than Lure of the Flames but it's not THAT much weaker.<br /> <br /> . </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it a little more: Thaumaturgy being so limited makes sense within the context of V5 disciplines (Generally weaker, everything's 1-5, Thaumaturgy would go from seeming OP to being actually OP if it retained it's old functionality). It makes sense in the new context.<br /> But I don't like the new context. You yourself stated you missed 6+ disciplines.<br /> And from a fluff perspective, yeah, it's terrible. It's one-true-wayism to an extreme, it demonstrates a misunderstanding of who the Tremere and Assamite sorcerers are (or were), it creates a gulf between the mechanics and the fluff that wasn't there before, it has created a sizable loss of old capabilities. It recontextualizes the Tremere and Assamite sorcerers within their respective societies (That caste system existed, even if I think it was too strict, and now it is silly) and also it's just... way less fun in my opinion. Variety was meant to be the spice of a Thaumaturge's unlife. Also the old stuff was just better written, and thaumaturgy earned itself an entire trilogy just for deeper exploration; you couldn't do that with new thaumaturgy: There aren't even enough avenues of research to justify a single chantry.<br /> <br /> This edition was not-very-nice to Assamites, Tremere, Lasombra, Settites, Necromancers... Some of the less human clans, I might add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T12:04:27-07:00","id":1418222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1417687#post1417687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I hate those bloody Keepers and Magisters. You're lucky I didn't make them afraid of the dark as well. <br /> <br /> In seriousness, this is an interesting discussion, but I would urge people to credit the writers and developers with at least a modicum of sense, and keep in mind the metaplot is in part designed with the long game in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very long game, because we don't even have mechanical support for, nor rumours of a release date for The Sabbat book(s), they don't fit the morality mechanics (unless they end up even more bowlderised and on Humanity en mass...which begs they question of why have them at all, the Paths is what is fascinating about them, and nothing I have read thus far gets within a hundred miles of that, certainly not the cults, definitely not what I have heard about the 9 Fires, and not the write ups of the defecting Lasombra) nor the themes that have been emphasised this edition <br /> <br /> So their may be a grand plan, but it doesn't look hopeful so far, at least not in a recognisable and interesting form, but then I didn't like the direction Revised started them on, or the declaration that they were a degenerate sect, by the person who now has ultimate say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-14-2020, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T12:27:41-07:00","id":1418226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's all a big scam so the elders can kill of their neonates in shipping crates and join the nuCamarilla. Calling it (well, I called it before but...)<br /> Anything else is silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's a scam, it's a really shitty one. In THE CAMARILLA, its said that the Sabbat is exterminating the Elders of the organization that have been Beckoned. They said they are LOSING the Gehenna War. Which makes sense because the Camarilla have no access to the police, money, or industry they rely on. They just have their raw Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the book I've read on the topic suggested that although the sabbat understoon the basics of how Camarilla society works, much of the intricacies and perculiarities of courts elude them and cause them to stick out. In the example given, I think you would get caught trying to 'find the Lasombra'; an established Lasombra would probably lobby elysium to take place with no or few mirrors, or they'd avoid the non-essential Elysiums in places with many (and if you're using the V5 weakness, it's a little harder to find them stick out) and going around trying to look into something reflective or using a bug is undoubtedly something that will be noticed by the absurdly keen eyes of the auspex users there. If the prince is particularly paranoid and the entree is suspicious (Say, they have no relfection) there are tests they can be subjected to. The question on if the intruder survives the night is really up to the court: They may lose face if the Lasombra Antitribu dies to a Sabbat Assassin. It might be in their personal interests to turn a blind eye to a potential killing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, what I'm saying is:<br /> <br /> * Lasombra Antitribu will stick out like a sore thumb in any Camarilla city.<br /> * The Sabbat will send a vampire to the city they're staying in, probably Antitribu<br /> * All they have to do is announce themselves as their Clan in the Modern Nights. Like, &quot;Hi, I'm Dave of Clan Brujah.&quot;<br /> * Then Dave will eliminate the Lasombra Antitribu and disappear back into the night.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla's previous claims of open-door policy to all Kindred means the Sabbat can just walk in and burrow into their society until they need to do their mission.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you wouldn't send a Lasombra to infiltrate a Camarilla domain. That'd be silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418222#post1418222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very long game, because we don't even have mechanical support for, nor rumours of a release date for The Sabbat book(s), they don't fit the morality mechanics (unless they end up even more bowlderised and on Humanity en mass...which begs they question of why have them at all, the Paths is what is fascinating about them, and nothing I have read thus far gets within a hundred miles of that, certainly not the cults, definitely not what I have heard about the 9 Fires, and not the write ups of the defecting Lasombra) nor the themes that have been emphasised this edition<br /> <br /> So their may be a grand plan, but it doesn't look hopeful so far, at least not in a recognisable and interesting form, but then I didn't like the direction Revised started them on, or the declaration that they were a degenerate sect, by the person who now has ultimate say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, some of this is flat out not true.<br /> <br /> * The spiritualism and in-depth occult examination of Kindred theology that the Paths TOUCHED on is greatly expanded in Blood Gods. If you like the fluff of the Paths, the Blood Cults utterly blow them away. No one can actually say otherwise and give an argument without just getting into rules technicalities.<br /> <br /> * The Seven Fires are just the Sabbat. They aren't very well detailed but they're as terrifying and dangerous as ever. They're just in hiding around Chicago.<br /> <br /> * What themes are you referring to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-14-2020, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T15:35:32-07:00","id":1418256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418024#post1418024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because Sabbat agents are smarter than Camarilla ones. There's entire books about Sabbat infiltrators and they will fool Camarilla Primogens and Princes 9/10. The &quot;open door policy&quot; of the Camarilla almost always ends in the Sabbat's favor.<br /> <br /> Sabbat infiltrators almost ALWAYS accomplish their mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I think every ST needs to determine for themselves because I always found this idea to be stupid. Princes just don't acknowledge whoever shows up in their domain. They have the power to refuse admission. Nor does acknowledgment simply require a vampire to give their name and clan, and the Prince accepts it at face value like a chump. It's more like an interview collecting lots of personal data that can be verified later. Who is their sire? How long have they been a vampire? What were there past domains? Who can vouch for their character? And there's likely a probationary period where a new vampire is allowed to stay, but not truly acknowledged while things get checked out. And during this time they are watched by ghouls, mortal servants, and the Prince's henchmen and allies.<br /> <br /> I think this gets overlooked by a lot of STs and PCs because people want to move on with the game, but that's actually what would happen. Different Princes and different domains will vary in terms of their strictness and leniency, but you can bet when it appears any threat rises, Princes become more strict. The Sabbat Crusades of the 1960s would have put everyone on alert for the next few decades.<br /> <br /> While all sects have their geniuses and fools, in general a vampire does not get to be Prince unless they're smart and cunning. So this idea the Sabbat can easily infiltrate is just dumb. No system is fool proof, so infiltration can and does happen. But I don't find the idea credible that Sabbat infiltrators always accomplish their mission. There's a lot of risk. Some fail. And to make a mission succeed, the Sabbat needs to spend time and resources to enable it to happen so even success has its cost. And if you burn a long time deep cover agent to accomplish something, there's extensive opportunity costs.<br /> <br /> In general, the game has often relied on the idea that NPCs are stupid in order to make the metaplot work. This was very true in Revised. But it makes for bad movies, and it makes for a bad RPG setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T16:02:36-07:00","id":1418259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418256#post1418256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something I think every ST needs to determine for themselves because I always found this idea to be stupid. Princes just don't acknowledge whoever shows up in their domain. They have the power to refuse admission. Nor does acknowledgment simply require a vampire to give their name and clan, and the Prince accepts it at face value like a chump. It's more like an interview collecting lots of personal data that can be verified later. Who is their sire? How long have they been a vampire? What were there past domains? Who can vouch for their character? And there's likely a probationary period where a new vampire is allowed to stay, but not truly acknowledged while things get checked out. And during this time they are watched by ghouls, mortal servants, and the Prince's henchmen and allies.<br /> <br /> I think this gets overlooked by a lot of STs and PCs because people want to move on with the game, but that's actually what would happen. Different Princes and different domains will vary in terms of their strictness and leniency, but you can bet when it appears any threat rises, Princes become more strict. The Sabbat Crusades of the 1960s would have put everyone on alert for the next few decades.<br /> <br /> While all sects have their geniuses and fools, in general a vampire does not get to be Prince unless they're smart and cunning. So this idea the Sabbat can easily infiltrate is just dumb. No system is fool proof, so infiltration can and does happen. But I don't find the idea credible that Sabbat infiltrators always accomplish their mission. There's a lot of risk. Some fail. And to make a mission succeed, the Sabbat needs to spend time and resources to enable it to happen so even success has its cost. And if you burn a long time deep cover agent to accomplish something, there's extensive opportunity costs.<br /> <br /> In general, the game has often relied on the idea that NPCs are stupid in order to make the metaplot work. This was very true in Revised. But it makes for bad movies, and it makes for a bad RPG setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books are very clear that vampires are an extremely secretive and isolationist species. A lot of vampires don't know how many Clans there are or what their names are, let alone the detailed knowledge the Players have from reading the books. Certainly, there's no database of how many vampires or who they are about. A vampire introduces themselves as Fred and says he's the childe of Dave, there is no way to verify this. Any vampire who is stupid enough to try to assemble a name and description of every vampire in their domain, let alone for the rest of the Kindred race, will be set out for the sun.<br /> <br /> I always emphasized the Sabbat's infiltrators and covert agents in my games, though. I felt Sabbat undermining the stability of domains and converting people was a big part of their appeal. The shovelheads and vozhd never appealed to me versus the crafty shadow wars.<br /> <br /> Personally, I always felt it was a mistake to make the Lasombra so belligerent to their Antitribu and that the Lasombra should have always had a substantial presence in the organization. However, that was the depiction as presented in the previous books. I feel like the depiction in V5 is a course correction and moves canon in the right direction.<br /> <br /> But YMMV.<br /> <br /> I do find it funny a lot of people seem to have thought the numbers were always what V5 is making them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T17:49:19-07:00","id":1418272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418259#post1418259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books are very clear that vampires are an extremely secretive and isolationist species. A lot of vampires don't know how many Clans there are or what their names are, let alone the detailed knowledge the Players have from reading the books. Certainly, there's no database of how many vampires or who they are about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to completely disagree again. There are lots of counter evidence that show a vampire can do this, and that vampires do try. Perhaps not some fledgling or neonate, but for any experienced ancillae or Prince this should be quite trivial. For the Prince, this is a major part of his job. Even if he doesn't know off the bat, he'll probably receive an &quot;education&quot; from the local Primogen or a visiting Archon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418259#post1418259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vampire introduces themselves as Fred and says he's the childe of Dave, there is no way to verify this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I see such a presentation go down.<br /> <br /> <i>Prince: &quot;OK, Dave, childe of Fred, why do you seek to enter my domain? Where did you previously come from and how long were you there previously?&quot;<br /> <br /> Dave: &quot;I'm not going to answer that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Prince: &quot;Fine, get out. If you are seen again in this city after sundown tomorrow, the Sheriff or Scourge will deal with you. I'm letting the Primogen, the Harpies, and all my allies that I denied you admission to this domain and circulate the picture of you my security cameras captured. You better leave my domain immediately. Don't be caught here after tonight. I'll have my Sheriff escort you outside tonight and drop you off 50 miles outside the city limits on the main highway.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> <i>Dave: &quot;I, um, wanted to see new sights and find a more hospitable place. I previous lived in, um, Omaha.&quot;<br /> <br /> Prince: &quot;Excellent, we'll now move on to the remaining portion of the interview...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> LATER<br /> <br /> <i>Prince: &quot;So what did the Prince of Omaha say on the phone when you mentioned that Dave, childe of Fred, had moved to my domain?&quot;<br /> <br /> Seneschal: &quot;He said he knew no such vampire. Furthermore, he doesn't know anyone named Fred either. Since I also happened to meet the Brujah Primogen of Omaha from that Conclave ten years ago, I sent a message to her. She said he had not heard of any such vampire either - even among the local Anarchs. I then contacted Archon Jones about this. He said he had heard other local Princes reported a similar looking vampire show up in their domain, but using a different alias. He always gave unverifiable information as well, so they denied him entry.&quot;<br /> <br /> Prince: &quot;This is good. My ghoul watching the Regency hotel reported Dave returned for the night, but then moved out. I had another retainer waiting outside shadow him, and we know what haven he is using tonight. What do you think I should do? Have him staked and brought back here for questioning as to why he lied? Or just destroyed outright during the day?&quot;<br /> <br /> Seneschal: &quot;Normally I would say stake him. I'd like to know what he's trying to pull. But because of (that Lasombra anti-tribu who moved here recently, or the Sabbat Crusades on the East Coast, or the Anarchs have gotten too frisky, etc.), we should just have the ghouls torch him once the sun comes up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Prince: &quot;Excellent, I agree.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> DAVE GETS DRAGGED OUT INTO THE SUN BY SOME GHOULS THE NEXT MORNING AND IS INCINERATED UNDER THE SUN.<br /> <br /> I can do lots of variations on that, emphasizing any number of things or how obstacles might be overcome.<br /> <br /> The idea that the Prince of a city, or some other vampire assisting him, doesn't know how to contact other important vampires is just ludicrous. Even if all he knows is the contact information of an Archon serving on the same continent, that Archon knows enough people to make calls and get responses to the Prince in a reasonable amount of time. Not all Archons need to be warriors. Some will specialize in Masquerade preserving activities. Others are glorified secretaries and bureaucrats for their Justicars who keeps tabs on people.<br /> <br /> Now there's going to be a fair amount of non-Sabbat vampires who can't answer all questions well. Maybe he's a Gangrel abandoned by his sire (who was subsequently destroyed), or a Brujah illegally embraced, a spurned Caitiff of uncertain ancestry, or something else that will cause that vampire trouble. Even in those cases, he'll likely have some kind of reputation where he's from, someone who knows him and can vouch for him. He may be in probationary status for a longer time, or harassed, or told to get out and he needs to wander somewhere else until he finds some craphole he can stay in and build a reputation. But he can likely give answers that won't immediately cause him to get kicked out, killed, or put under permanent suspicion. Or if he does, its tough luck for him. He'll eventually fall among Anarchs who are the ones who actually don't care. Or maybe gets killed by Lupines. Or runs afoul of the Sabbat or mortal hunters. But it's his bad luck, not that of the Camarilla or the local Prince. It also fits in historically with why certain clans always complained about the Camarilla harassing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418259#post1418259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any vampire who is stupid enough to try to assemble a name and description of every vampire in their domain, let alone for the rest of the Kindred race, will be set out for the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally the job of the Prince according to the Traditions of Domain and Hospitality. There will be lots of things a Prince doesn't know about in his domain, but any Kindred presenting himself for acceptance in the domain is going to get a lot of questions. And even if there are vampires who are never presented the Prince in the city, the Prince likely learns about them at some point (what he does about it is a different matter). Certainly in the smaller towns, this is completely doable. In larger cities, like canonical Chicago this is more difficult. But we know Lodin always struggled with this, but he never stopped trying.<br /> <br /> Vampires who show up and don't present themselves may be under the radar of a Prince for a long time. He can find the malcontents, discontented, and outright Anarchs. But he won't be showing up to Elysium or hanging out with respectable members of the Camarilla. And if or when his name and appearance gets reported to the Prince, the Prince will know this vampire entered his domain illegally.<br /> <br /> Information is power, and among vampires of the Camarilla even more so. I don't see this as being stupid or objectionable. This is expected and common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418259#post1418259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always emphasized the Sabbat's infiltrators and covert agents in my games, though. I felt Sabbat undermining the stability of domains and converting people was a big part of their appeal. The shovelheads and vozhd never appealed to me versus the crafty shadow wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer a more subtle approach myself. But that doesn't mean I make the Princes and Camarilla loyalists stupid in order to do so.<br /> <br /> I do think some Sabbat infiltrators do succeed. But I don't think it's easy, and it takes a lot of work. And they probably don't do it on a short-term tactical basis either. Its for long term deep cover agents who can be activated when absolutely needed. Most Sabbat spies aren't infiltrators, but the two man scout teams like Wendy and Philippe in CbN 1st who observe secretly and try to avoid interacting with other vampires.<br /> <br /> In general, I like how you describe how you run your games. But this is definitely one area I think is flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T18:00:30-07:00","id":1418275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418272#post1418272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I like how you describe how you run your games. But this is definitely one area I think is flawed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, fair enough, but I do like the idea that Princes are islands of their own domain. Most vampires don't know who lives in their city beyond the Prince and Sheriff (and only the Prince really knows everyone who lives in the city). Lineages are now almost all forgotten with only a few able to name their lineage back up to Caine or someone recognizable, especially in America. I may be overselling how easy it is to infiltrate in a Prince's city, though.<br /> <br /> Either way, it doesn't matter much since V5 has flooded the Camarilla with Lasombra.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T18:59:28-07:00","id":1418281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418275#post1418275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, fair enough, but I do like the idea that Princes are islands of their own domain. Most vampires don't know who lives in their city beyond the Prince and Sheriff (and only the Prince really knows everyone who lives in the city). Lineages are now almost all forgotten with only a few able to name their lineage back up to Caine or someone recognizable, especially in America. I may be overselling how easy it is to infiltrate in a Prince's city, though.<br /> <br /> Either way, it doesn't matter much since V5 has flooded the Camarilla with Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of your approaches may work depending on how old and savvy the individual Prince is. Also, I generally feel like European Princes would both be more knowledgeable and have a better intelligence system than their American cousins (insert Lincoln joke lol).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-14-2020, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T22:17:45-07:00","id":1418301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418226#post1418226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, some of this is flat out not true.<br /> <br /> * The spiritualism and in-depth occult examination of Kindred theology that the Paths TOUCHED on is greatly expanded in Blood Gods. If you like the fluff of the Paths, the Blood Cults utterly blow them away. No one can actually say otherwise and give an argument without just getting into rules technicalities.<br /> <br /> * The Seven Fires are just the Sabbat. They aren't very well detailed but they're as terrifying and dangerous as ever. They're just in hiding around Chicago.<br /> <br /> * What themes are you referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Those ' technicalities ' are core to the point, the Cults are expensive backgrounds, afaik, they aren't the unbending core of identity that holds back the beast that the Paths are, they are human style religion for vampires, maybe that religion is a personality cult, maybe it's mystery cult, big deal it doesn't replace humanity like the Paths.<br /> <br /> The Seven Fires are first edition style mindless, boring terrorists, yay, who cares they could be Anarchs for all their motives matter.<br /> <br /> For themes: this edition is hunger as the all conquering core theme, not morality the Path/Road system has been crippled to the extent of not mattering, so what makes the Sabbat interesting, that iron will holding back the beast doesn't fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-15-2020, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T22:21:32-07:00","id":1418302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418301#post1418301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Those ' technicalities ' are core to the point, the Cults are expensive backgrounds, afaik, they aren't the unbending core of identity that holds back the beast that the Paths are, they are human style religion for vampires, maybe that religion is a personality cult, maybe it's mystery cult, big deal it doesn't replace humanity like the Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your issue is purely systematic.<br /> <br /> I've always preferred the Paths as sets of beliefs over the Heiriarchy of Sins.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I really wish someone would create a V20 style &quot;Path of Mithras&quot; based on the religion described in Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> I think it would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T22:50:56-07:00","id":1418304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418302#post1418302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your issue is purely systematic.<br /> <br /> I've always preferred the Paths as sets of beliefs over the Heiriarchy of Sins.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I really wish someone would create a V20 style &amp;quot;Path of Mithras&amp;quot; based on the religion described in Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> I think it would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The systems are the setting, oh another flaw, you still have human touchstones, I don't care if that human is someone you hideously mistreat, it is still passing off your morality to a human. <br /> <br /> The Hierarchy is the in rules representation of belief, an deeply personal and internal thing made manifest on paper and in rules, in a way the cults utterly fail at (from what I have managed to.glean without the book) .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T22:54:09-07:00","id":1418305,"title":"","content":"Paths have me re-wire my brain for play. They are fantastic. I think a few have tenets that don't work or need interpretation (The first published path of paradox is suicidal), but on the whole there is something so wonderful about choosing and adopting new morality. And there's something hilarious about finding yourself commiting an atrocoty whilst worrying about the moral risk of something normal people find trivial. <br /> <br /> Creating a cult is pretty easy. Besides I've always thought the Camarilla was filled with cults, knightly orders and secret societies , too numerous and too protean to list entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T23:38:00-07:00","id":1418309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418304#post1418304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The systems are the setting, oh another flaw, you still have human touchstones, I don't care if that human is someone you hideously mistreat, it is still passing off your morality to a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like they should add some more rules to the Touchstones and hope they do in the Players Guide. Touchstones should be there to make keeping your Humanity easier, not as an essential part of it.<br /> <br /> The idea is good but Requiem did Touchstones much-much better.<br /> <br /> You should have vampires have a material benefit to act like vampires in fiction: obsessed and stalking mortals like Bella, Buffy, and Mina. However, you should also have other kinds of touchstones like Churches, Organizations, or even other vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T02:24:26-07:00","id":1418323,"title":"","content":"I feel it's worth noting:<br /> <br /> Obtenebration is not welcome in the Camarilla: It's a masquerade destroyer, it's heavily associated with the sect's enemies who often reject humanity, and a good chunk of Camarilla leadership are closet Noddists who don't like vampires using anything that wasn't used by Caine IE the common disciplines, protean and thaumaturgy. Vicissitude is certainly worse (they are <i>never</i> joining the Camarilla) but Obtenebration is <i>bad</i>. Camarilla Lasombra are probably embarrassed by the discipline, really.<br /> <br /> Oblivion... ehhh... It's a lot harder to fear it, really. Also since everything's getting amalgamated the Noddist argument probably doesn't really hold up so well. I suppose when Vicissitude gets foolishly turned into Protean the Tzmisce can come aboard to and we can all hold hands and run in a circle and sing kumbaya...<br /> <br /> <br /> *Yes, the Sabbat are noddists, but as they are lead by the two clans with horrifying disciplines that Caine certainly didn't use, so their noddist interpretations are certainly going to lie more with 'These disciplines are fine but Caine's disciplines are cooler' instead of the closet hatred of the Camarilla's -we claim dominion to all vampires but we're going to begin by giving representation and favouritism to the clans with orthodox disciplines- (Malkavians had only Dominate at that point)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T04:20:11-07:00","id":1418337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418226#post1418226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * The Seven Fires are just the Sabbat. They aren't very well detailed but they're as terrifying and dangerous as ever. They're just in hiding around Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious about what you find so terrifying about the seven fires,<br /> if anything their write up made me laugh,<br /> <br /> I'm thinking you're more terrified by your own headcanon or interpretation of them rather than whatever's written in the book<br /> <br /> plus, you just said &quot;The shovelheads and vozhd never appealed to me versus the crafty shadow wars.&quot;, and I don't see how the seven fires match in anyway your preferences<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * The spiritualism and in-depth occult examination of Kindred theology that the Paths TOUCHED on is greatly expanded in Blood Gods. If you like the fluff of the Paths, the Blood Cults utterly blow them away. No one can actually say otherwise and give an argument without just getting into rules technicalities. </div> </div> </div>is there any section in Cult of the Blood Gods dedicated to the sabbat religious paradigm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T08:18:09-07:00","id":1418367,"title":"","content":"To be honest, the Sabbat was stretching suspension of disbelief further and further. It is like that XKCD webcomic graphing Bigfoot sightings against the number of mobile phones with cameras out in the population. The Sabbats percentage of shovelheads and official policy of disregarding the Masquerade was just not sustainable. Too many cameras out there now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418259#post1418259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books are very clear that vampires are an extremely secretive and isolationist species. A lot of vampires don't know how many Clans there are or what their names are, let alone the detailed knowledge the Players have from reading the books. Certainly, there's no database of how many vampires or who they are about. A vampire introduces themselves as Fred and says he's the childe of Dave, there is no way to verify this. Any vampire who is stupid enough to try to assemble a name and description of every vampire in their domain, let alone for the rest of the Kindred race, will be set out for the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the authors of the <i>Encyclopedia Vampirica</i>, <i>Encyclopedia Haemovoria</i>, etc seems to have done ok, and not actually been set out for the sun. What you are describing sounds more like the situation of a low-information Caitiff, not someone who has actually been taught the basics by their sire. And there is actually an entire Tradition about keeping tabs on who is in your domain, the Fifth Tradition.<br /> <br /> Not every kindred will have dots in Kindred lore, but not knowing the Clans sounds like a flaw.<br /> <br /> It would also bring up the question of what the Justicars and Archons actually do with their nights, if the Kindred are that information-poor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:03:23-07:00","id":1418370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418367#post1418367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, the Sabbat was stretching suspension of disbelief further and further. </div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat is a magic trick; it's this thing where on the surface it shouldn't work, but it does. The Sabbat has it's own logistics for the Masquerade, it just doesn't want to acknowledge them (and in a Camarilla city, it's abusing the Camarilla's logistics; they're doing all the work for them) <br /> Also generally humans suck <i>in the world of darkness</i> and wouldn't believe the truth if you merged their brain with a computer and fucking programmed them to. There's so much distracting noise out there, so much fake news, so much bullshit, and everyone's deluded themselves into thinking they're too smart to believe in magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:08:27-07:00","id":1418371,"title":"","content":"If people don't mind me responding with bullet points rather than specifics:<br /> <br /> 1. I feel like nitpicking over Disciplines is going to be a bit weird for the Camarilla to do, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a>. There's a lot to hate the Lasombra defectors over but I don't think citing the Book of Nod and Caine not having Obternation is going to be one of them. I actually agree with you that Obternation was nerfed a too much, though. When I mentioned that I loved playing Lucita-types, I meant that literally as there's nothing more awesome than being the tiny pale black-haired girl with her army of shadow monsters and doom tendrils. The discipline just doesn't lend itself to those kind of horrors anymore. You're right that the rules as is make it a Masquerade and Humanity draining work, though. I don't support Obternation giving stains as is, though. You need to USE it for evil, IMHO.<br /> <br /> 2. I think the <b>Seven Fires</b> aren't detailed enough to give much of an opinion on. They aren't something that has gotten it's own Blood Cult write-up yet. What I like is purely from what I consider to be a preview, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a>. What we got in <i>The Chicago Folio</i> was a teaser, really. My take on them is they emphasize the fact the Sabbat are terrifying and secretive with the ability to move in and out of Kindred society almost completely unseen. Yes, they're engaged in acts of literal terrorism (defined here as, &quot;horrifying inhuman deeds designed to sap the moral of and frighten their enemies&quot;) but that's a well-known way for an army deprived of strong military force to destroy a larger one's capacity to rule. You know, if they're assholes. V5 is much grittier, darker, and morally ambiguous than previous editions so it's good to see the Sabbat are the people who go the farthest. We also have a mystery as to what they're about. But the big benefit of the S7 is the fact that we know they EXIST and thus the Sabbat having forces carrying on the good work is canon. Which justifies the Storytellers doing any Sabbat games they want.<br /> <br /> 3. Like I said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2471\" data-vbnamecard=\"2471\">Trollroot</a>, I overstated matters but I do strongly believe that if a Prince knows the vampires of another city then that other city's Prince has done something wrong. They are to handle the accounting of their domain and to make sure they have the Masquerade firmly under control. Archons, Justicars, and so on will ride into town and deal with any problems that emerge but I can't imagine Madame Guile knows the name of Gengis or Anita Wainwright until someone hands her a file--and they're the local troublemakers' leaders. The Nosferatu certainly might have access to their information and will gladly sell it to them but they also have to access local resources like the Prince and Elders. But YMMV.<br /> <br /> 4. As for the &quot;not knowing clans&quot; thing, it's mostly because of The Chicago Folio and other supplements that seem to go, &quot;And Shejana belongs to a long dead Clan that we don't speak of anymore.&quot; When, yes, my initial reaction would be, &quot;You mean the Ravnos? The guys gone just twenty years ago?&quot; I feel like V5 was ramping up the mysteriousness of the Independent Clans that was how they were originally portrayed in 2nd Edition. Most licks on the street didn't know anything about the Sabbat or Independent Clans. In Night Road, they have canonized it further when your character reacts to the Sabbat as, &quot;What the hell is the Sabbat?&quot;<br /> <br /> 5. Ideology-wise, the Sabbat has always been less of a specific Blood Cult itself and more a collection of Blood Cults all under one banner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-15-2020, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T10:11:51-07:00","id":1418389,"title":"","content":"You are supposed to be <i>afraid</i> of exotic disciplines:<br /> Dementation makes you mad, Diamonion's the devil, Vicissitude is evil demonic space alien disease that violates the holy immutable form of the Cainite race, and Obtenebration summons unknowable horror from a realm Hostile to all of God's creation. <br /> <br /> Now, from the perspective of people from these clans, this might be just stuff they say so that outsiders don't covet their special gifts. But It shouldn't take much for a very conservative Camarilla Noddist to fear and loath degenerate evil disciplines, Especially when your bible says &quot;these ones are what Good ol' Caine had&quot; and maybe your Apocrypha says 'Vicissitude was what happened when a 2nd generation vampire tried to seperate all the evil from himself through Protean and it went into a mortal that he embraced out of curiosity' or 'Lasombra stole Obtenebration from Lilith's demonic garden of horror' (Yeah, this is all stuff i've read, not making that up) <br /> Add the fact that in the Camarilla, you've been pretty sheltered from all these horrible heretical disciplines. Also all the people you've heard of that use these powers are sick evil fucks. Your sire probably told you horror stories. You don't know any Tzmisce well, and the few meetings you've had probably just confirmed your biases.<br /> <br /> Imagine you're the kind of Camarilla Elder who hires a scourge because you think killing the pathetic thin bloods will stave off the apocalyptic event of your great x8 grandsire's rise to eat all her children. <br /> Yeah, Nah; The Lasombra and their freaky ink discipline can fuck right off<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">-Also you get to feel smug and superior for having wholesome all-natural Caine disciplines- </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T14:16:50-07:00","id":1418413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418367#post1418367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, the Sabbat was stretching suspension of disbelief further and further. It is like that XKCD webcomic graphing Bigfoot sightings against the number of mobile phones with cameras out in the population. The Sabbats percentage of shovelheads and official policy of disregarding the Masquerade was just not sustainable. Too many cameras out there now.</div> </div> </div> </div>then give vampires better disciplines to hide<br /> <br /> the sabbat doesn't disregard the masquerade, they just don't enforce it on neonates, which is one way they protect the &quot;freedom&quot; of neonates because neonates can't masquerade for shit and depend too much on their elders,<br /> the sabbat is also allowed to handle masquerade breaches whichever way they like,<br /> since they are not restricted by humanity (we're playing vampires, remember?) they can abuse dominate, murder, fleshcraft whatever to cover the breach<br /> <br /> if you don't like it, give the neonates better powers, and you won't have to worry about them breaking the masquerade that often","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-15-2020, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],