title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T14:22:59-07:00","id":1418417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417630-what-do-you-think-of-the-lasombra-joining-the-camarilla-in-v5?p=1418371#post1418371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people don't mind me responding with bullet points rather than specifics:<br /> <br /> 1. I feel like nitpicking over Disciplines is going to be a bit weird for the Camarilla to do, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a>. There's a lot to hate the Lasombra defectors over but I don't think citing the Book of Nod and Caine not having Obternation is going to be one of them. I actually agree with you that Obternation was nerfed a too much, though. When I mentioned that I loved playing Lucita-types, I meant that literally as there's nothing more awesome than being the tiny pale black-haired girl with her army of shadow monsters and doom tendrils. The discipline just doesn't lend itself to those kind of horrors anymore. You're right that the rules as is make it a Masquerade and Humanity draining work, though. I don't support Obternation giving stains as is, though. You need to USE it for evil, IMHO.<br /> <br /> 2. I think the <b>Seven Fires</b> aren't detailed enough to give much of an opinion on. They aren't something that has gotten it's own Blood Cult write-up yet. What I like is purely from what I consider to be a preview, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a>. What we got in <i>The Chicago Folio</i> was a teaser, really. My take on them is they emphasize the fact the Sabbat are terrifying and secretive with the ability to move in and out of Kindred society almost completely unseen. Yes, they're engaged in acts of literal terrorism (defined here as, &quot;horrifying inhuman deeds designed to sap the moral of and frighten their enemies&quot;) but that's a well-known way for an army deprived of strong military force to destroy a larger one's capacity to rule. You know, if they're assholes. V5 is much grittier, darker, and morally ambiguous than previous editions so it's good to see the Sabbat are the people who go the farthest. We also have a mystery as to what they're about. But the big benefit of the S7 is the fact that we know they EXIST and thus the Sabbat having forces carrying on the good work is canon. Which justifies the Storytellers doing any Sabbat games they want.<br /> <br /> 3. Like I said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2471\" data-vbnamecard=\"2471\">Trollroot</a>, I overstated matters but I do strongly believe that if a Prince knows the vampires of another city then that other city's Prince has done something wrong. They are to handle the accounting of their domain and to make sure they have the Masquerade firmly under control. Archons, Justicars, and so on will ride into town and deal with any problems that emerge but I can't imagine Madame Guile knows the name of Gengis or Anita Wainwright until someone hands her a file--and they're the local troublemakers' leaders. The Nosferatu certainly might have access to their information and will gladly sell it to them but they also have to access local resources like the Prince and Elders. But YMMV.<br /> <br /> 4. As for the &quot;not knowing clans&quot; thing, it's mostly because of The Chicago Folio and other supplements that seem to go, &quot;And Shejana belongs to a long dead Clan that we don't speak of anymore.&quot; When, yes, my initial reaction would be, &quot;You mean the Ravnos? The guys gone just twenty years ago?&quot; I feel like V5 was ramping up the mysteriousness of the Independent Clans that was how they were originally portrayed in 2nd Edition. Most licks on the street didn't know anything about the Sabbat or Independent Clans. In Night Road, they have canonized it further when your character reacts to the Sabbat as, &quot;What the hell is the Sabbat?&quot;<br /> <br /> 5. Ideology-wise, the Sabbat has always been less of a specific Blood Cult itself and more a collection of Blood Cults all under one banner.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blood Cult write ups are.shallow at best, sorry Paths deserve far better. (This may ofc improve but so far...yuck and meh).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":".  Words 10-15-2020, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T14:23:04-07:00","id":1418418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classi